{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:37:33.410Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6f3879884d552ec7</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_G4aejTWceU5PX0qqn07cPaaB</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\4e98c32a-1d17-48da-bc15-302ae5043fea\\tasks\\a6f3879884d552ec7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Finish guard cleanup\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Phase 2 finished. Nothing committed, nothing pushed.\n\n## The REFERR-GATE report was stale\nNo `PickerScreenMatch` exists anywhere in the tree. The prior agent had already renamed it `PromptScreenMatch` and rewired the live `/v1/message` helpers before the 403. `(REFERR-GATE)` now runs clean across all 7 shipped packages — 0 dangerous diagnostics. No dead answer-guard types were restored.\n\n## Changes made\n\n**`packages/host-service/src/companion/read-api.ts`** — fixed the 2 real type errors the prior agent left: `terminalPiercesCuration` took `ReadonlySet&lt;string&gt;` but `visible` is `Map&lt;string, HostWorkspaceRow&gt;` → now `ReadonlyMap&lt;string, HostWorkspaceRow&gt;`. Moved the two call-site comments onto the helper. Verified the prior agent's deletion of `if (!visible.has(row.id) &amp;&amp; all.length === 0) continue;` is genuinely redundant — `all.length === 0` implies `shown.length === 0`, which the unconditional `continue` 6 lines later already handles.\n\n**`packages/host-service/src/companion/answer.ts`** — removed dead import `provenMultiSelectFreeTextDetectLabels` (guard-5's only consumer). Collapsed `matchPromptStillOnScreen`, a pure one-line pass-through, into `matchPromptOnScreen`. Deleted the orphaned step-9 comment claiming an agent-binding refusal that no longer has code and is contradicted by the `(ANSWER-GUARDLESS)` note directly under it. Rewrote stale references to removed machinery: `readGuardSource` (gone), `(GUARD5-ANCHOR)` → `(PICKER-CHROME)`, `(GUARD5-ROW-ANCHOR)`, `(GUARD4-ABSTAIN)` on `baseAudit`, \"Guard 5's source\" on `snapshotScreen`, \"guard 5's capture-derived anchors\".\n\n**`packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts`** — removed the orphaned 20-line `GUARD 6 / (ASKQ-MARKER-READ)` docblock that the prior agent left stranded above `log()`, and the `toolResultExists` docblock left stranded above `agentBinding`. Retitled the `GUARD 3` / `GUARD 4` adapter labels to say what they actually are (`/v1/message` only). Fixed \"guard 4\", \"guard 9\", \"guard 1\", \"guard 2\", \"guard-5 snapshot\" references.\n\n**`packages/host-service/src/companion/types.ts`** — the prior agent's new `ANSWER_GUARD_NAMES` comment was wrong: it said the set is legacy-read-only, but `session` is still emitted live by `/v1/message` as a `GuardFailedDetail`. Corrected, and restored the `(LEDGER-COHERENCE)` tag (the family still exists in `attempt-ledger.ts`). Made the `guardsPassed`/`guardsAbstained`/`guards` wire docs honest — they described an evaluation that no longer happens.\n\n**`packages/host-service/src/companion/question-store.ts`** — the prior agent's replacement comment claimed `PendingQuestion.agentId` is \"retained for internal ownership diagnostics\". Nothing reads it. Replaced with an honest note (validated at the capture boundary, currently unread, only consumer was the retired `.askq` guard).\n\n**`packages/host-service/src/terminal/terminal.ts`** — the prior agent's `writableSession` extraction silently changed the acknowledged-write error from `\"Terminal session not prepared\"` to `\"Terminal session not found\"`, a string the companion answer path surfaces to a phone. Restored via an `absentError` default param. Also removed a redundant second map lookup it introduced in `prepareAcknowledgedInputSession` (`getOrAdoptSession` already returns the session and already checks the workspace).\n\n## Deleted tests — verdict\n\n`picker-screen.test.ts` tested only `matchPickerScreen`, which no longer exists. It never touched a live helper. Deleting it lost nothing. Confirmed by history: `screenShowsPickerChrome` and `handleMessage` have **never** had a test in this repo.\n\n`guard-abstain.test.ts` **did** lose live coverage — its `(ANSWER-GUARDLESS) a replayed answer` block covered `ledgerRecordToResponse`, which is still live and explicitly documented as \"exported for the replay contract test\". Restored as 4 focused tests in `answer-guardless.test.ts`.\n\nNew file: **`packages/host-service/src/companion/picker-chrome.test.ts`** (126 lines, 14 tests, untracked — needs staging). `screenShowsPickerChrome` is the last thing between a phone message and a bare `\\r` in an open picker, it just went through a large refactor, and it had zero coverage. Pins the deliberate asymmetry (must-match: live picker, unbounded gaps, digit-decoy continuation lines, box drawing; must-not-match: descending order, mid-line numbers, multi-digit markers, single row).\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `(REFERR-GATE)` | clean, 7/7 packages |\n| host-service `tsc` | 1 error, pre-existing |\n| Feature markers | 147/147 |\n| `bun test src/companion/` | 200 pass, 0 fail (12 files) |\n| `bun test src/terminal/` | 87 tests, 4 fail — all pre-existing |\n| `tmp/answer-guardless-probe.test.ts` | 11 pass, 0 fail |\n| Scoped Biome (40 files) | clean |\n\n**Pre-existing diagnostics, proven not mine** by running `tsc` and the tests in a throwaway worktree at HEAD (`ec83cf8e4`), then removing it:\n- `src/terminal/terminal.ts(2902,49) TS2554: Expected 1 arguments, but got 2` — `portManager.checkOutputForHint`, ~1900 lines from anything touched.\n- 4 `src/terminal/env.test.ts` failures (`resolveLaunchShell`, `getShellLaunchArgs`) — POSIX shell paths asserted on Windows. Fail identically at HEAD.\n\nBiome also flagged an unsorted-import error the prior agent introduced in `answer.ts` (`AcknowledgedInputFailureKind` inserted mid-block); fixed with a scoped `--write`. New file's git blob verified pure LF.\n\n## Deliberately skipped\n\n1. **`Keystroke.expect` / `ScreenExpectation` are now write-only.** Set by `encodeAnswer`, read by nothing — `injectSequence` is guardless. Removing them ripples through `keystrokes.ts` and three keystroke test files. Real dead weight, but well past this diff.\n2. **`provenMultiSelectFreeTextDetectLabels()` + `multiSelectFreeTextRowDetectLabels`** are now orphaned (guard-5 was the sole consumer). Left intact: `keystrokes.ts` is gated by two FEATURES.md markers and its contents are recorded measurements against a real CLI build — deleting proven-contract data is a maintainer call.\n3. **`guardsAbstained` values are inconsistent across the seven outcome sites** in `handleAnswer` (some `null`, some `[]`). Type-legal — `AnswerAttemptRecord` requires an array, `AuditEntry` allows null — but the distinction no longer carries meaning. Unifying them changes persisted audit content, so I corrected the comment instead.\n4. **Six exported tunables have no external consumer** (`LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS`, `MESSAGE_ECHO_*`, etc.). Pre-existing, unrelated to the guard removal.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>235644</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>146</tool_uses><duration_ms>2623628</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
