marker script previously falsely reported all markers missing in one Windows run:\n     - Direct `git grep` proved marker presence.\n     - Later Opus validation reported `147/147`.\n\n   - GitHub workflow dispatch initially hit:\n     ```text\n     HTTP 404: workflow build-arm64.yml not found on the default branch\n     ```\n     - `gh` inferred upstream.\n     - Fixed by explicitly supplying:\n       ```text\n       --repo khairm/superset-windows-arm64\n       ```\n\n   - First cleanup fork failed with API/Cloudflare error:\n     ```text\n     Please run /login\n     API Error: 403\n     Unable to load site\n     ```\n     - The fork had already edited the shared working tree.\n     - The user then explicitly requested Opus subagents.\n     - A plain Opus subagent continued from those edits and completed the cleanup.\n\n   - Partial cleanup temporarily left:\n     ```text\n     src/companion/answer.ts(...): error TS2304:\n     Cannot find name 'PickerScreenMatch'\n     ```\n     - Opus confirmed the eventual report was stale after the type had been correctly replaced with `PromptScreenMatch`.\n     - Fresh `(REFERR-GATE)` passed 7/7 packages.\n\n   - Partial curation helper used wrong container type:\n     - `ReadonlySet<string>` versus actual `Map<string, HostWorkspaceRow>`.\n     - Fixed to `ReadonlyMap<string, HostWorkspaceRow>`.\n\n   - Initial shared terminal helper changed an externally visible error:\n     - `\"Terminal session not prepared\"` became `\"Terminal session not found\"`.\n     - Opus restored the original semantic distinction with an `absentError` parameter.\n\n   - Incorrect Bun cwd syntax:\n     ```text\n     bun --cwd packages/pty-daemon run build:daemon\n     ```\n     printed Bun usage.\n     - Corrected to:\n       ```text\n       bun run --cwd \"$PWD/packages/pty-daemon\" build:daemon\n       ```\n     - Bundle build then passed.\n\n   - Initial full cleanup build was not the first build:\n     - Build `31437447650` succeeded on `ec83cf8e4`, but did not include `/simplify`.\n     - A replacement build `31443284669` was triggered for `7e0d25f3c`.\n     - Replacement build completed successfully.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   Completed and pushed:\n\n   - Removed all production answer eligibility guards.\n   - Preserved only the exact current-question/fingerprint synchronous write arbitration.\n   - Made pending questions visible independent of capability/session and curation.\n   - Added daemon-level acknowledged PTY writes.\n   - Added durable outcome readback.\n   - Contained audit persistence failures.\n   - Fixed unreadable transcript caching.\n   - Added honest ambiguous-first-write fencing.\n   - Added detached-session preparation/adoption.\n   - Added protocol-v2 compatibility and protocol-v3 acknowledgments.\n   - Fixed protocol-v2 answer truncation with whole-sequence fallback.\n   - Fixed positive transcript settlement races.\n   - Aligned heartbeat/tree discovery.\n   - Deleted the retired answer guard stack and tests.\n   - Preserved `/v1/message` protections.\n   - Added focused picker-chrome tests.\n   - Completed `/simplify`.\n   - Completed `/code-review low` with no findings.\n   - Pushed both commits to `main`.\n   - Published a successful Windows ARM64 installer.\n\n   Commits:\n\n   ```text\n   ec83cf8e4 fix(host-service): make companion answers guardless and durable\n   7e0d25f3c refactor(host-service): remove retired answer guards\n   ```\n\n   Build results:\n\n   - Initial guardless build:\n     - run: `31437447650`\n     - SHA: `ec83cf8e40bf26fa05d3cdd03136930acfd0d55e`\n     - conclusion: success\n     - URL:\n       `https://github.com/khairm/superset-windows-arm64/actions/runs/31437447650`\n   - Final cleanup build:\n     - run: `31443284669`\n     - SHA: `7e0d25f3c0ecec91324b5302b265674269800cac`\n     - conclusion: success\n     - URL:\n       `https://github.com/khairm/superset-windows-arm64/actions/runs/31443284669`\n\n   Validation after final Opus cleanup:\n\n   - `(REFERR-GATE)`:\n     - clean across all 7 shipped packages\n   - Host-service TypeScript:\n     - only accepted pre-existing TS2554\n   - Feature markers:\n     - `147/147`\n   - Full companion suite:\n     - `200 pass`\n     - `0 fail`\n     - 12 files\n   - Scratch guardless fault probe:\n     - `11 pass`\n     - `0 fail`\n   - Focused final answer/picker/probe run:\n     - `38 pass`\n     - `0 fail`\n     - `87 expect() calls`\n   - PTY protocol/handler run:\n     - `29 pass`\n     - `0 fail`\n     - `73 expect() calls`\n   - PTY daemon bundle:\n     - passed\n   - Scoped Biome:\n     - clean\n   - Override consistency:\n     - passed\n   - Unified versions:\n     - `1.20.0`\n   - `git diff --check` / staged diff check:\n     - clean apart from expected autocrlf warnings\n   - `/code-review low 7e0d25f3c`:\n     - no findings\n   - Repository working tree was clean after commit/push.\n\n   Existing local terminal-test debt:\n\n   - 87 terminal tests with 4 failures.\n   - Opus proved all 4 fail identically at clean `ec83cf8e4`.\n   - They are Windows/POSIX shell expectation failures in `env.test.ts`.\n\n   `/simplify` findings deliberately skipped because fixes would change behavior or exceed safe scope:\n\n   - generic DaemonClient request/reply helper\n   - incremental transcript parsing\n   - parallel transcript scanning\n   - curation-provenance redesign\n   - removal of measured picker-contract detection data\n   - removal of `Keystroke.expect`/`ScreenExpectation`\n   - unifying persisted `guardsAbstained` content\n   - changing unrelated exported tunables\n\n6. All User Messages:\n\n   Genuine earlier user messages preserved from the prior context:\n\n   - `/compact`\n   - “This desktop is too old to answer this kind of question from here. i didn't answer the existing adams email thread still open for an hour and it gave me this. I didn't approve this barrier. remove all barriers, if I can answer in the terminal I want the phone to be able to handle it. end of story, stop building stupid safety mechanisms for this 1 person app”\n   - “i typed in an askuser and gpt yhis Unconfirmed - the desktop accepted the write but did not confirm the outcome”\n   - “This may or may not have gone through. Nothing will be sent again - checking reads the outcome from the desktop... this is bullshit how far can it be to type in a box... why are we getting these errors.. the question remained unanswered still I'm gonna do it on desktop now... make sure everything has heavy logging so you can tackle everything 1st shot”\n   - Empty multi-select decision:\n     - “Refuse w/ message (Recommended)”\n   - “I couldn't even respond on my watch it said desktop bridge wouldn't allow - wtf is this man... I need to kill all barriers to my perfect ux - follow simple rule if there is a question in terminal I need to be able to answer phone or watch - no blockers without my explciti approval per blocker (currently I want none and we add over time)”\n   - Desktop installation decision at that earlier point:\n     - “Later”\n   - Biometric decision:\n     - “Drop biometric gate (Recommended)”\n   - ADB endpoints:\n     - “phone 56:40921    watch 67:39025”\n   - Updated phone endpoint:\n     - “56:46199”\n   - Earlier installer authorization:\n     - “Install now (Recommended)”\n   - “all installed now - do you need to do e2e testing on your emulated versions etc?”\n   - `/compact`\n   - “Continue from where you left off.”\n   - Screenshot complaint:\n     - “dude what is this? I thought you I told you to get rid of all the guards. it's killing the ux. I need to be able to respond. In every scenario no matter what. that chat is still open so you can emulate right now. I wanted to choose option one if you need to test.”\n   - “it needs to work even if the screen is off and I need to enter my password to open it again”\n   - “get sol and fable to thoroughly review the approach - use emulators to test where possible”\n   - “please confirm that this issue will be resolved as well. by this, you better make sure from logs that you're really tackling the root cause ux comes first. these guards need to be killed off... generally make sweeping changes to kill the odds of my messages not being able to get through”\n   - “if you need to test that question is still open, I'd like to choose the option that gives us a one-off script in the CWD”\n   - Security constraint:\n     - “Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.”\n   - Never touch production database unless explicitly requested and confirmed.\n   - Ship only through the full GitHub Windows ARM64 build/release path.\n   - Never hot-patch.\n   - Install only after explicit authorization at the exact time.\n   - Do not add answer UX barriers without explicit user approval.\n\n   User messages in this continuation:\n\n   - A continuation message containing the previous compaction summary and:\n     - “Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly...”\n   - `/simplify`, requiring:\n     - Phase 0 gather the diff\n     - Phase 1 four independent parallel review agents\n     - Phase 2 deduplicate and directly apply valid findings\n   - “you ok?”\n   - Interrupted request followed by:\n     - “use opus sub agents to continue”\n   - Installer decision:\n     - “Install now (Recommended)”\n   - Current request:\n     - “CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.”\n     - Asked for this detailed `<analysis>` and `<summary>` compaction response.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\n   Code and build shipment are complete.\n\n   Installation verification is pending:\n\n   - Confirm detached installer process completed.\n   - Confirm Superset restarted.\n   - Confirm installed version/build corresponds to:\n     - `desktop-v1.20.0`\n     - commit `7e0d25f3c0ecec91324b5302b265674269800cac`\n   - Do not claim installation success before observing it.\n\n   Required post-install E2E:\n\n   - Inspect detached daemon migration and negotiated protocol.\n   - Verify protocol v3 acknowledgment is active after restart.\n   - If a protocol-v2 daemon is encountered, verify whole-sequence unconfirmed migration behavior.\n   - Run the phone protocol emulator against the shipped bridge.\n   - Locate or create a real pending Claude question.\n   - Answer from the physical phone.\n   - Answer from the physical watch.\n   - Test with renderer hidden/unavailable.\n   - Test with display off.\n   - Test with Windows locked or at login screen.\n   - Verify daemon acknowledgment logs.\n   - Verify durable answer ledger outcome.\n   - Verify no answer path emits `guard_failed`.\n   - Verify a complete multi-keystroke answer during any v2 transition.\n   - Preserve the no-sensitive-logging rule.\n   - ADB wireless-debugging ports rotate; obtain current phone/watch endpoints before physical-device work and verify device identity with `getprop ro.product.model`.\n\n   Optional remaining E2E gap from earlier work:\n\n   - Physical watch free-text dictation remains unit-tested/code-reviewed but was not previously live-tested.\n\n   Task state:\n\n   - Task #3, “Verify and ship the guardless path,” was marked completed because:\n     - code was committed\n     - review passed\n     - main was pushed\n     - the full publish build succeeded\n   - Post-install E2E is a remaining operational verification step, not an unshipped code task.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Immediately before this summary request:\n\n   1. The final build was already green:\n      ```text\n      run 31443284669\n      headSha 7e0d25f3c0ecec91324b5302b265674269800cac\n      conclusion success\n      ```\n\n   2. The user was shown an interactive installation decision explaining that installation would close Superset and the current session.\n\n   3. The user explicitly selected:\n      ```text\n      Install now (Recommended)\n      ```\n\n   4. The published release was inspected:\n      ```text\n      desktop-v1.20.0\n      Superset-1.20.0-arm64.exe\n      sha256:a42f6715ee58849fbb018f262a6a8a7d14b3906ca451c9b910d7d7af792a96e3\n      ```\n\n   5. The installer was downloaded to:\n      `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\guardless-install\\Superset-1.20.0-arm64.exe`\n\n   6. The local SHA-256 matched the GitHub release digest exactly.\n\n   7. The installer was launched detached:\n      ```text\n      installer launched pid 1704515\n      ```\n\n   8. No subsequent observation confirmed:\n      - installer completion\n      - app restart\n      - installed version\n      - post-install daemon migration\n      - phone/watch answer E2E\n\n   Therefore, the accurate current state is:\n\n   - Installer launch: confirmed.\n   - Digest integrity: confirmed.\n   - Installation completion: not yet confirmed.\n   - Post-install E2E: not yet run.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Resume directly after Superset restarts and verify installation before making any success claim.\n\n   Relevant recent quotes:\n\n   - User authorization:\n     - “Install now (Recommended)”\n   - Last observed action:\n     - “installer launched pid 1704515”\n\n   Direct next sequence:\n\n   1. Confirm the installer exited successfully and Superset restarted.\n   2. Confirm the running installed app is `desktop-v1.20.0` built from `7e0d25f3c`.\n   3. Inspect host-service and PTY daemon protocol/liveness logs without exposing sensitive content.\n   4. Run the shipped bridge’s phone-emulator closed-loop answer test.\n   5. Obtain current physical phone/watch ADB endpoints before physical-device checks.\n   6. Run the real phone/watch and Windows locked/display-off E2E matrix.\n   7. Report separately:\n      - what was genuinely end-to-end\n      - what was synthetic/emulated\n      - whether acknowledgment and durable settlement were observed\n      - whether any answer result emitted `guard_failed`\n\n   Do not install again unless a new exact-time authorization is needed; the user already authorized and the installer has already been launched once.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"783f3da3-a2f5-43e1-85c4-d745f1ef1602","timestamp":"2026-08-12T01:48:19.104Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
