tion index 0 exactly once using sealed real companion protocol; never log/write free-text question bodies, option labels, answers, keys, tokens, JWTs, transcript content, decrypted tree/question/answer bodies, or crypto material. Output only non-sensitive metadata: HTTP status, opaque questionId/requestId, protocol version, question count/shape counts, outcome/error code. Use an innocuous single-select answer so no free-text. Preserve Cloudflare/hello/crypto boundary internally but do not print secrets. Fail fast. Put script in tmp/phone-emu/emu-safe.ts and/or a safe driver. Do not touch production files. Validate syntax. Return exact command to run in background and expected output. Do not execute the answer.","outputFile":"C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a48b8b8fc05312ec1.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"17578b50-ffa6-4f42-bbd7-5f126df3a30b","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T02:17:00.660Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"emulator-prep\">\nExact recommended orchestration after YOU create the redacted throwaway harness at `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\phone-emu\\closed_loop_safe.py`:\n\n1. Arm in the background (yes, this works; it polls while AskUser blocks):\n`uv run python \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/tmp/phone-emu/closed_loop_safe.py\"`\nRun via Bash/PowerShell with `run_in_background:true` and a 420s timeout. The safe script should internally execute `bun run tmp/phone-emu/emu-safe.ts ...` from repo root and print only phase/result metadata.\n\n2. Immediately issue ONE real AskUserQuestion in this same main terminal/session with exactly one single-select question and two options:\n- header: `E2E check`\n- question: `Which test result should the companion submit?`\n- multiSelect: `false`\n- option 0 label: `Pass E2E`\n- option 0 description: `Selects the expected test outcome.`\n- option 1 label: `Fail E2E`\n- option 1 description: `Selects the alternate test outcome.`\nThe safe harness must dynamically detect that new pending question and submit option index 0 exactly once. This avoids any free-text body and exercises the simplest proven picker byte contract.\n\n3. Safe output contract: only `{phase,httpStatus,questionId,questionCount,answerable,requestId,outcome,coverageEpoch,status}`; no question text/header/descriptions/option labels/fingerprint, decrypted bodies, JWT, key refs, device IDs, nonces, terminal snapshots, or transcript content. It may log opaque IDs needed for DB correlation, but avoid dumping complete envelopes/bodies.\n\n4. DB proof command concept (run read-only through a small `bun:sqlite`/existing DB utility; output selected columns only): query `answer_attempts WHERE request_id=?`, require confirmed + resolved timestamp + lease, null failure, `guards_passed_json='[]'`. Re-run the status read with the same requestId/coverageEpoch—never resend `/v1/answer`.\n\nDo NOT use unchanged `closed_loop.py`, `closed_loop3.py`, or `emu.ts --quiet`; all still persist or print decrypted question/tree data. I did not execute or edit anything.\n</agent-message>"}
