{"parentUuid":"026edcef-21b0-48f2-859a-9860174ce8cf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44611460-2829-462e-b2e9-af8e653be0db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_RiEc9ssS7PA31YgTxFAZTmio","type":"tool_result","content":"3240\t\t| {\n3241\t\t\t\tkind: \"unconfirmed\";\n3242\t\t\t\treason: string;\n3243\t\t\t\tabortedAt: number;\n3244\t\t\t\twritten: number;\n3245\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: AnswerGuardName[];\n3246\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: AnswerGuardName[];\n3247\t\t\t\tevaluation: GuardEvaluation;\n3248\t\t  };\n3249\t\n3250\t/**\n3251\t * Runs entirely inside the per-terminal lock.\n3252\t *\n3253\t * Before EVERY keystroke: the lease is re-verified and renewed, the emulator\n3254\t * mirror is proven to have caught up with the previous byte, a fresh snapshot is\n3255\t * taken, and the full guard stack is evaluated against THAT snapshot. Only then\n3256\t * is the byte written.\n3257\t *\n3258\t * There is no compensating action on a mid-sequence abort. Sending Escape to\n3259\t * \"clean up\" would be another blind byte against a screen we just admitted we\n3260\t * cannot characterise. We stop, and we say the outcome is unknown.\n3261\t */\n3262\tasync function injectSequence(\n3263\t\tdeps: AnswerDeps,\n3264\t\tinput: {\n3265\t\t\tquestion: PendingQuestion;\n3266\t\t\thost: HostTerminalRef;\n3267\t\t\tkeystrokes: readonly Keystroke[];\n3268\t\t\tleaseId: string;\n3269\t\t\twriter: RawPtyWriter;\n3270\t\t},\n3271\t): Promise<InjectionResult> {\n3272\t\tconst { question, host, keystrokes, leaseId, writer } = input;\n3273\t\tconst deadlineMs = deps.now() + SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS;\n3274\t\n3275\t\tlet written = 0;\n3276\t\tlet previousScreen: string | null = null;\n3277\t\tlet guardsPassed: AnswerGuardName[] = [];\n3278\t\t/** (GUARD4-ABSTAIN) Carried beside `guardsPassed`, never merged into it. */\n3279\t\tlet guardsAbstained: AnswerGuardName[] = [];\n3280\t\tlet evaluation: GuardEvaluation = {\n3281\t\t\ttranscript: false,\n3282\t\t\tscreen: false,\n3283\t\t\tbinding: false,\n3284\t\t\tpermission_axis: false,\n3285\t\t\tsession: false,\n3286\t\t\taskq_marker: false,\n3287\t\t};\n3288\t\n3289\t\t/**\n3290\t\t * The one fork every abandonment takes: nothing landed => the guard-style\n3291\t\t * refusal the client knows how to show; something landed => `unconfirmed`,\n3292\t\t * which is never downgraded to a failure.\n3293\t\t *\n3294\t\t * `guard` is a PARAMETER rather than a constant. Most call sites here are not\n3295\t\t * guard failures at all — a lapsed lease, the sequence deadline, a mirror that\n3296\t\t * never repainted — and they report `session` because that is what they share\n3297\t\t * with a client: this terminal is not in a state we can safely write to. That\n3298\t\t * used to be hardcoded, so a reader of the `guard_failed` result could not\n3299\t\t * tell a genuine guard 3 failure from a deadline. Now each site says which\n3300\t\t * name it is reporting under, and the mid-sequence guard failure passes the\n3301\t\t * guard that actually failed instead of rebuilding this same fork inline.\n3302\t\t */\n3303\t\tconst abort = (\n3304\t\t\treason: string,\n3305\t\t\tindex: number,\n3306\t\t\tguard: AnswerGuardName,\n3307\t\t): InjectionResult =>\n3308\t\t\twritten === 0\n3309\t\t\t\t? {\n3310\t\t\t\t\t\tkind: \"guard_failed\",\n3311\t\t\t\t\t\tguard,\n3312\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed,\n3313\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained,\n3314\t\t\t\t\t\tevaluation,\n3315\t\t\t\t\t}\n3316\t\t\t\t: {\n3317\t\t\t\t\t\tkind: \"unconfirmed\",\n3318\t\t\t\t\t\treason,\n3319\t\t\t\t\t\tabortedAt: index,\n3320\t\t\t\t\t\twritten,\n3321\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed,\n3322\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained,\n3323\t\t\t\t\t\tevaluation,\n3324\t\t\t\t\t};\n3325\t\n3326\t\tfor (let index = 0; index < keystrokes.length; index += 1) {\n3327\t\t\tconst keystroke = keystrokes[index];\n3328\t\t\tif (keystroke === undefined) {\n3329\t\t\t\treturn abort(\"missing keystroke\", index, \"session\");\n3330\t\t\t}\n3331\t\n3332\t\t\tif (deps.now() >= deadlineMs) {\n3333\t\t\t\treturn abort(\"sequence deadline exceeded\", index, \"session\");\n3334\t\t\t}\n3335\t\n3336\t\t\t// The lease can lapse mid-sequence. Renewing must be able to FAIL, or we\n3337\t\t\t// would keep typing into a question another device has taken over.\n3338\t\t\tconst extension = deps.leases.extend(leaseId, deps.now());\n3339\t\t\tif (!extension.ok) {\n3340\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n3341\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.lease_lost\",\n3342\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: question.questionId,\n3343\t\t\t\t\tleaseId,\n3344\t\t\t\t\treason: extension.reason,\n3345\t\t\t\t\tkeystrokeIndex: index,\n3346\t\t\t\t});\n3347\t\t\t\treturn abort(`lease ${extension.reason}`, index, \"session\");\n3348\t\t\t}\n3349\t\n3350\t\t\t// Prove the mirror reflects our previous byte before trusting it. Without\n3351\t\t\t// this, guard 5 could pass against a repaint that has not happened yet.\n3352\t\t\tif (previousScreen !== null) {\n3353\t\t\t\tconst advanced = await awaitScreenAdvance(\n3354\t\t\t\t\tdeps,\n3355\t\t\t\t\tquestion.terminalId,\n3356\t\t\t\t\tpreviousScreen,\n3357\t\t\t\t\tMath.min(deadlineMs, deps.now() + SCREEN_ADVANCE_TIMEOUT_MS),\n3358\t\t\t\t);\n3359\t\t\t\tif (advanced === null) {\n3360\t\t\t\t\treturn abort(\n3361\t\t\t\t\t\t\"screen did not advance after the previous keystroke\",\n3362\t\t\t\t\t\tindex,\n3363\t\t\t\t\t\t\"session\",\n3364\t\t\t\t\t);\n3365\t\t\t\t}\n3366\t\t\t\t// (ADVANCE-SCREEN-DISCARDED) `advanced` IS DELIBERATELY NOT REUSED as\n3367\t\t\t\t// the guard's screen, and the redundant snapshot below is the point.\n3368\t\t\t\t//\n3369\t\t\t\t// `awaitScreenAdvance` returns the FIRST snapshot that differs from the\n3370\t\t\t\t// previous one, which proves the TUI consumed our byte — it does not\n3371\t\t\t\t// prove the repaint finished, and a half-drawn frame is exactly the\n3372\t\t\t\t// input guard 5's matcher must not be handed. Reusing it would also\n3373\t\t\t\t// widen the gap between \"what we observed\" and \"what we then wrote\n3374\t\t\t\t// into\" by up to one poll interval, on the one guard §11.3 lists as\n3375\t\t\t\t// load-bearing. One extra viewport snapshot per keystroke is the price\n3376\t\t\t\t// of evaluating guard 5 against the freshest screen there is.\n3377\t\t\t}\n3378\t\n3379\t\t\tconst screen = await safeSnapshot(deps, question.terminalId);\n3380\t\t\tif (screen === null) {\n3381\t\t\t\t// Guard 5 is load-bearing; an unreadable screen is not a reason to\n3382\t\t\t\t// proceed, it is the reason not to.\n3383\t\t\t\treturn abort(\"screen snapshot unavailable\", index, \"session\");\n3384\t\t\t}\n3385\t\t\tconst outcome = await evaluateGuards(deps, {\n3386\t\t\t\tquestion,\n3387\t\t\t\tscreen,\n3388\t\t\t\texpectation: keystroke.expect,\n3389\t\t\t\trequireOptionIndex: keystroke.optionIndex,\n3390\t\t\t});\n3391\t\t\t// Attempt-wide evidence, not last-keystroke evidence. See\n3392\t\t\t// `mergeAttemptEvidence`.\n3393\t\t\t({ guardsPassed, guardsAbstained, evaluation } = mergeAttemptEvidence(\n3394\t\t\t\tindex === 0 ? null : { guardsPassed, guardsAbstained, evaluation },\n3395\t\t\t\toutcome,\n3396\t\t\t));\n3397\t\n3398\t\t\tif (outcome.failed !== null) {\n3399\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n3400\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.guard_failed\",\n3401\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: question.questionId,\n3402\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n3403\t\t\t\t\tguard: outcome.failed,\n3404\t\t\t\t\tguardClass: GUARD_CLASSES[outcome.failed],\n3405\t\t\t\t\tkeystrokeIndex: index,\n3406\t\t\t\t\twritten,\n3407\t\t\t\t\tscreenReason: outcome.screenMatch?.reason ?? null,\n3408\t\t\t\t\tscreenMissing: outcome.screenMatch?.missing ?? null,\n3409\t\t\t\t\t// First-shot diagnosis: the complete per-guard picture at the failing\n3410\t\t\t\t\t// keystroke, not just the name of the guard that tripped.\n3411\t\t\t\t\texpectation: keystroke.expect.kind,\n3412\t\t\t\t\tevaluation: { ...outcome.evaluation },\n3413\t\t\t\t\tpassed: [...outcome.passed],\n3414\t\t\t\t\tabstained: [...outcome.abstained],\n3415\t\t\t\t});\n3416\t\t\t\treturn abort(\n3417\t\t\t\t\t`guard ${outcome.failed} failed mid-sequence`,\n3418\t\t\t\t\tindex,\n3419\t\t\t\t\toutcome.failed,"}]},"uuid":"a6746654-9a9d-40de-af6f-29ac2ad41d32","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:16:42.380Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\answer-with-advance.ts","content":"\t| {\n\t\t\tkind: \"unconfirmed\";\n\t\t\treason: string;\n\t\t\tabortedAt: number;\n\t\t\twritten: number;\n\t\t\tguardsPassed: AnswerGuardName[];\n\t\t\tguardsAbstained: AnswerGuardName[];\n\t\t\tevaluation: GuardEvaluation;\n\t  };\n\n/**\n * Runs entirely inside the per-terminal lock.\n *\n * Before EVERY keystroke: the lease is re-verified and renewed, the emulator\n * mirror is proven to have caught up with the previous byte, a fresh snapshot is\n * taken, and the full guard stack is evaluated against THAT snapshot. Only then\n * is the byte written.\n *\n * There is no compensating action on a mid-sequence abort. Sending Escape to\n * \"clean up\" would be another blind byte against a screen we just admitted we\n * cannot characterise. We stop, and we say the outcome is unknown.\n */\nasync function injectSequence(\n\tdeps: AnswerDeps,\n\tinput: {\n\t\tquestion: PendingQuestion;\n\t\thost: HostTerminalRef;\n\t\tkeystrokes: readonly Keystroke[];\n\t\tleaseId: string;\n\t\twriter: RawPtyWriter;\n\t},\n): Promise<InjectionResult> {\n\tconst { question, host, keystrokes, leaseId, writer } = input;\n\tconst deadlineMs = deps.now() + SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS;\n\n\tlet written = 0;\n\tlet previousScreen: string | null = null;\n\tlet guardsPassed: AnswerGuardName[] = [];\n\t/** (GUARD4-ABSTAIN) Carried beside `guardsPassed`, never merged into it. */\n\tlet guardsAbstained: AnswerGuardName[] = [];\n\tlet evaluation: GuardEvaluation = {\n\t\ttranscript: false,\n\t\tscreen: false,\n\t\tbinding: false,\n\t\tpermission_axis: false,\n\t\tsession: false,\n\t\taskq_marker: false,\n\t};\n\n\t/**\n\t * The one fork every abandonment takes: nothing landed => the guard-style\n\t * refusal the client knows how to show; something landed => `unconfirmed`,\n\t * which is never downgraded to a failure.\n\t *\n\t * `guard` is a PARAMETER rather than a constant. Most call sites here are not\n\t * guard failures at all — a lapsed lease, the sequence deadline, a mirror that\n\t * never repainted — and they report `session` because that is what they share\n\t * with a client: this terminal is not in a state we can safely write to. That\n\t * used to be hardcoded, so a reader of the `guard_failed` result could not\n\t * tell a genuine guard 3 failure from a deadline. Now each site says which\n\t * name it is reporting under, and the mid-sequence guard failure passes the\n\t * guard that actually failed instead of rebuilding this same fork inline.\n\t */\n\tconst abort = (\n\t\treason: string,\n\t\tindex: number,\n\t\tguard: AnswerGuardName,\n\t): InjectionResult =>\n\t\twritten === 0\n\t\t\t? {\n\t\t\t\t\tkind: \"guard_failed\",\n\t\t\t\t\tguard,\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed,\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained,\n\t\t\t\t\tevaluation,\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t: {\n\t\t\t\t\tkind: \"unconfirmed\",\n\t\t\t\t\treason,\n\t\t\t\t\tabortedAt: index,\n\t\t\t\t\twritten,\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed,\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained,\n\t\t\t\t\tevaluation,\n\t\t\t\t};\n\n\tfor (let index = 0; index < keystrokes.length; index += 1) {\n\t\tconst keystroke = keystrokes[index];\n\t\tif (keystroke === undefined) {\n\t\t\treturn abort(\"missing keystroke\", index, \"session\");\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif (deps.now() >= deadlineMs) {\n\t\t\treturn abort(\"sequence deadline exceeded\", index, \"session\");\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// The lease can lapse mid-sequence. Renewing must be able to FAIL, or we\n\t\t// would keep typing into a question another device has taken over.\n\t\tconst extension = deps.leases.extend(leaseId, deps.now());\n\t\tif (!extension.ok) {\n\t\t\tdeps.log({\n\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.lease_lost\",\n\t\t\t\tquestionId: question.questionId,\n\t\t\t\tleaseId,\n\t\t\t\treason: extension.reason,\n\t\t\t\tkeystrokeIndex: index,\n\t\t\t});\n\t\t\treturn abort(`lease ${extension.reason}`, index, \"session\");\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Prove the mirror reflects our previous byte before trusting it. Without\n\t\t// this, guard 5 could pass against a repaint that has not happened yet.\n\t\tif (previousScreen !== null) {\n\t\t\tconst advanced = await awaitScreenAdvance(\n\t\t\t\tdeps,\n\t\t\t\tquestion.terminalId,\n\t\t\t\tpreviousScreen,\n\t\t\t\tMath.min(deadlineMs, deps.now() + SCREEN_ADVANCE_TIMEOUT_MS),\n\t\t\t);\n\t\t\tif (advanced === null) {\n\t\t\t\treturn abort(\n\t\t\t\t\t\"screen did not advance after the previous keystroke\",\n\t\t\t\t\tindex,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"session\",\n\t\t\t\t);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t// (ADVANCE-SCREEN-DISCARDED) `advanced` IS DELIBERATELY NOT REUSED as\n\t\t\t// the guard's screen, and the redundant snapshot below is the point.\n\t\t\t//\n\t\t\t// `awaitScreenAdvance` returns the FIRST snapshot that differs from the\n\t\t\t// previous one, which proves the TUI consumed our byte — it does not\n\t\t\t// prove the repaint finished, and a half-drawn frame is exactly the\n\t\t\t// input guard 5's matcher must not be handed. Reusing it would also\n\t\t\t// widen the gap between \"what we observed\" and \"what we then wrote\n\t\t\t// into\" by up to one poll interval, on the one guard §11.3 lists as\n\t\t\t// load-bearing. One extra viewport snapshot per keystroke is the price\n\t\t\t// of evaluating guard 5 against the freshest screen there is.\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tconst screen = await safeSnapshot(deps, question.terminalId);\n\t\tif (screen === null) {\n\t\t\t// Guard 5 is load-bearing; an unreadable screen is not a reason to\n\t\t\t// proceed, it is the reason not to.\n\t\t\treturn abort(\"screen snapshot unavailable\", index, \"session\");\n\t\t}\n\t\tconst outcome = await evaluateGuards(deps, {\n\t\t\tquestion,\n\t\t\tscreen,\n\t\t\texpectation: keystroke.ex