{"parentUuid":"6adda854-f7cd-4ab7-b042-2050a57f0ed1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44611460-2829-462e-b2e9-af8e653be0db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_dy14oN2X0ijXyr7ZSFqzYNf0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * (PICKER-CONTRACT-CANARY) Drive the REAL installed Claude Code in a pty and\n3\t * observe its AskUserQuestion picker through a headless emulator.\n4\t *\n5\t * Why the emulator: a raw pty stream carries cursor moves, not lines, so the\n6\t * \"screen\" only exists once something replays it. This is the same reconstruction\n7\t * the pty daemon's mode tracker does, which is what guard 5 reads in production —\n8\t * so what this prints is what the guard would see.\n9\t *\n10\t * Safe by construction: throwaway temp dir, never answers the question it raises\n11\t * (Esc, then interrupt, then kill), and the sanitized env keeps it off this\n12\t * session's gateway routing.\n13\t */\n14\t\n15\timport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\n16\timport * as os from \"node:os\";\n17\timport * as path from \"node:path\";\n18\timport ptyPkg from \"file:///C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/node_modules/.bun/@lydell+node-pty@1.1.0/node_modules/@lydell/node-pty/index.js\";\n19\tconst { spawn: ptySpawn } = ptyPkg;\n20\timport xtermPkg from \"file:///C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/node_modules/.bun/@xterm+headless@6.1.0-beta.289/node_modules/@xterm/headless/lib-headless/xterm-headless.js\";\n21\tconst { Terminal } = xtermPkg;\n22\t\n23\tconst COLS = 100;\n24\tconst ROWS = 40;\n25\tconst CLAUDE_EXE =\n26\t\t\"C:/Users/khair/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-code/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-code-win32-arm64/claude.exe\";\n27\t\n28\tconst multi = (process.argv[2] ?? \"single\") === \"multi\";\n29\tconst workdir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"picker-canary-\"));\n30\tconst outDir =\n31\t\t\"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/tmp/refusal-2026-08-08\";\n32\t\n33\tconst ask = `Use the AskUserQuestion tool RIGHT NOW, once, with exactly one question: header 'Canary', question 'Which canary option do you want for this run?', multiSelect ${multi ? \"true\" : \"false\"}, and exactly two options: label 'Yes' with description 'Enable the first canary option for this run.' and label 'Skip' with description 'Leave the second canary option alone entirely.' Do not use any other tool and do not write any files.`;\n34\t\n35\tconst env = {};\n36\tfor (const [key, value] of Object.entries(process.env)) {\n37\t\tif (value === undefined) continue;\n38\t\tif (/^(ANTHROPIC_|CLAUDE_|CLAUDECODE)/.test(key)) continue;\n39\t\tenv[key] = value;\n40\t}\n41\t\n42\tconst term = new Terminal({ cols: COLS, rows: ROWS, allowProposedApi: true });\n43\tconst pty = ptySpawn(CLAUDE_EXE, [\"--model\", \"sonnet\"], {\n44\t\tcwd: workdir,\n45\t\tcols: COLS,\n46\t\trows: ROWS,\n47\t\tname: \"xterm-256color\",\n48\t\tenv,\n49\t});\n50\tpty.onData((data) => {\n51\t\tterm.write(data);\n52\t});\n53\tlet exited = null;\n54\tpty.onExit((e) => {\n55\t\texited = `exitCode=${e.exitCode} signal=${String(e.signal)}`;\n56\t\tconsole.log(`[exit] ${exited}`);\n57\t});\n58\t\n59\tconst started = Date.now();\n60\t\n61\tfunction screen() {\n62\t\tconst buffer = term.buffer.active;\n63\t\tconst lines = [];\n64\t\tfor (let i = 0; i < buffer.length; i += 1) {\n65\t\t\tlines.push(buffer.getLine(i)?.translateToString(true) ?? \"\");\n66\t\t}\n67\t\treturn lines.join(\"\\n\");\n68\t}\n69\t\n70\t/** Wait for the emulator to settle, not just for bytes to arrive. */\n71\tfunction sleep(ms) {\n72\t\treturn new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));\n73\t}\n74\t\n75\tasync function waitFor(predicate, label, timeoutMs) {\n76\t\tconst deadline = Date.now() + timeoutMs;\n77\t\twhile (Date.now() < deadline) {\n78\t\t\tawait sleep(500);\n79\t\t\tif (predicate(screen())) {\n80\t\t\t\tconsole.log(`[+${Date.now() - started}ms] SAW ${label}`);\n81\t\t\t\treturn true;\n82\t\t\t}\n83\t\t}\n84\t\tconsole.log(`[+${Date.now() - started}ms] TIMEOUT ${label}`);\n85\t\treturn false;\n86\t}\n87\t\n88\tconst results = { variant: multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\" };\n89\t\n90\ttry {\n91\t\t// The trust prompt is about the temp dir this script just created.\n92\t\tif (\n93\t\t\tawait waitFor(\n94\t\t\t\t(t) => /Is this a project you created or one you trust/i.test(t),\n95\t\t\t\t\"trust prompt\",\n96\t\t\t\t30_000,\n97\t\t\t)\n98\t\t) {\n99\t\t\tpty.write(\"1\");\n100\t\t\tawait sleep(2_000);\n101\t\t\tresults.trustAccepted = true;\n102\t\t}\n103\t\n104\t\tconst ready = await waitFor(\n105\t\t\t(t) => /shortcuts|Welcome to Claude Code|Tips for getting started/i.test(t),\n106\t\t\t\"composer ready\",\n107\t\t\t45_000,\n108\t\t);\n109\t\tresults.ready = ready;\n110\t\tif (!ready) throw new Error(\"never reached the composer\");\n111\t\n112\t\tpty.write(ask);\n113\t\tawait sleep(1_200);\n114\t\tpty.write(\"\\r\");\n115\t\n116\t\tconst sawPicker = await waitFor(\n117\t\t\t(t) => /1\\.\\s*Yes/.test(t) && /2\\.\\s*Skip/.test(t),\n118\t\t\t\"picker rows 1. Yes / 2. Skip\",\n119\t\t\t180_000,\n120\t\t);\n121\t\tresults.sawPicker = sawPicker;\n122\t\n123\t\tif (sawPicker) {\n124\t\t\tconst text = screen();\n125\t\t\tfs.writeFileSync(\n126\t\t\t\tpath.join(outDir, `pty-picker-${multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\"}.txt`),\n127\t\t\t\ttext,\n128\t\t\t\t\"utf8\",\n129\t\t\t);\n130\t\t\tconst rows = text\n131\t\t\t\t.split(\"\\n\")\n132\t\t\t\t.map((line, index) => ({ index, line: line.trimEnd() }))\n133\t\t\t\t.filter((row) => /^[^0-9A-Za-z]*[1-9]\\.\\s\\S/.test(row.line));\n134\t\t\tresults.numberedRows = rows.map((row) => `${row.index}: ${row.line.trim()}`);\n135\t\t\tresults.freeTextExactSingle = /3\\.\\s+Type something\\./.test(text);\n136\t\t\tresults.freeTextNoPeriod = /3\\.\\s+Type something(?!\\.)/.test(text);\n137\t\t\tresults.anyFreeTextRow = /Type something/.test(text);\n138\t\t\tresults.chatRow = /Chat about this/.test(text);\n139\t\n140\t\t\tif (!multi && results.anyFreeTextRow === true) {\n141\t\t\t\tpty.write(\"3\");\n142\t\t\t\tresults.digitOpensEditor = await waitFor(\n143\t\t\t\t\t(t) => /Type something…/.test(t) || /Type something\\u2026/.test(t),\n144\t\t\t\t\t\"inline editor placeholder after digit 3\",\n145\t\t\t\t\t20_000,\n146\t\t\t\t);\n147\t\t\t\tfs.writeFileSync(\n148\t\t\t\t\tpath.join(outDir, \"pty-editor-single.txt\"),\n149\t\t\t\t\tscreen(),\n150\t\t\t\t\t\"utf8\",\n151\t\t\t\t);\n152\t\t\t\tpty.write(\"\\x1b\");\n153\t\t\t\tawait sleep(1_000);\n154\t\t\t\tresults.pickerBackAfterEsc = /1\\.\\s*Yes/.test(screen());\n155\t\t\t}\n156\t\t} else {\n157\t\t\tfs.writeFileSync(\n158\t\t\t\tpath.join(outDir, `pty-nopicker-${multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\"}.txt`),\n159\t\t\t\tscreen(),\n160\t\t\t\t\"utf8\",\n161\t\t\t);\n162\t\t}\n163\t} catch (error) {\n164\t\tresults.error = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n165\t\tresults.exited = exited;\n166\t\tfs.writeFileSync(\n167\t\t\tpath.join(outDir, `pty-fail-${multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\"}.txt`),\n168\t\t\tscreen(),\n169\t\t\t\"utf8\",\n170\t\t);\n171\t} finally {\n172\t\ttry {\n173\t\t\tpty.write(\"\\x1b\");\n174\t\t\tpty.write(\"\\x03\");\n175\t\t\tpty.write(\"\\x03\");\n176\t\t} catch {}\n177\t\tawait sleep(800);\n178\t\ttry {\n179\t\t\tpty.kill();\n180\t\t} catch {}\n181\t}\n182\t\n183\tconsole.log(JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));\n184\tprocess.exit(0);\n185\t"}]},"uuid":"875471a6-ebeb-43f7-ac49-801bdbabdbfe","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:17:12.647Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\refusal-2026-08-08\\pty_canary_node.mjs","content":"/**\n * (PICKER-CONTRACT-CANARY) Drive the REAL installed Claude Code in a pty and\n * observe its AskUserQuestion picker through a headless emulator.\n *\n * Why the emulator: a raw pty stream carries cursor moves, not lines, so the\n * \"screen\" only exists once something replays it. This is the same reconstruction\n * the pty daemon's mode tracker does, which is what guard 5 reads in production —\n * so what this prints is what the guard would see.\n *\n * Safe by construction: throwaway temp dir, never answers the question it raises\n * (Esc, then interrupt, then kill), and the sanitized env keeps it off this\n * session's gateway routing.\n */\n\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as os from \"node:os\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\nimport ptyPkg from \"file:///C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/node_modules/.bun/@lydell+node-pty@1.1.0/node_modules/@lydell/node-pty/index.js\";\nconst { spawn: ptySpawn } = ptyPkg;\nimport xtermPkg from \"file:///C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/node_modules/.bun/@xterm+headless@6.1.0-beta.289/node_modules/@xterm/headless/lib-headless/xterm-headless.js\";\nconst { Terminal } = xtermPkg;\n\nconst COLS = 100;\nconst ROWS = 40;\nconst CLAUDE_EXE =\n\t\"C:/Users/khair/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-code/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-code-win32-arm64/claude.exe\";\n\nconst multi = (process.argv[2] ?? \"single\") === \"multi\";\nconst workdir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"picker-canary-\"));\nconst outDir =\n\t\"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/tmp/refusal-2026-08-08\";\n\nconst ask = `Use the AskUserQuestion tool RIGHT NOW, once, with exactly one question: header 'Canary', question 'Which canary option do you want for this run?', multiSelect ${multi ? \"true\" : \"false\"}, and exactly two options: label 'Yes' with description 'Enable the first canary option for this run.' and label 'Skip' with description 'Leave the second canary option alone entirely.' Do not use any other tool and do not write any files.`;\n\nconst env = {};\nfor (const [key, value] of Object.entries(process.env)) {\n\tif (value === undefined) continue;\n\tif (/^(ANTHROPIC_|CLAUDE_|CLAUDECODE)/.test(key)) continue;\n\tenv[key] = value;\n}\n\nconst term = new Terminal({ cols: COLS, rows: ROWS, allowProposedApi: true });\nconst pty = ptySpawn(CLAUDE_EXE, [\"--model\", \"sonnet\"], {\n\tcwd: workdir,\n\tcols: COLS,\n\trows: ROWS,\n\tname: \"xterm-256color\",\n\tenv,\n});\npty.onData((data) => {\n\tterm.write(data);\n});\nlet exited = null;\npty.onExit((e) => {\n\texited = `exitCode=${e.exitCode} signal=${String(e.signal)}`;\n\tconsole.log(`[exit] ${exited}`);\n});\n\nconst started = Date.now();\n\nfunction screen() {\n\tconst buffer = term.buffer.active;\n\tconst lines = [];\n\tfor (let i = 0; i < buffer.length; i += 1) {\n\t\tlines.push(buffer.getLine(i)?.translateToString(true) ?? \"\");\n\t}\n\treturn lines.join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\n/** Wait for the emulator to settle, not just for bytes to arrive. */\nfunction sleep(ms) {\n\treturn new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));\n}\n\nasync function waitFor(predicate, label, timeoutMs) {\n\tconst deadline = Date.now() + timeoutMs;\n\twhile (Date.now() < deadline) {\n\t\tawait sleep(500);\n\t\tif (predicate(screen())) {\n\t\t\tconsole.log(`[+${Date.now() - started}ms] SAW ${label}`);\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tconsole.log(`[+${Date.now() - started}ms] TIMEOUT ${label}`);\n\treturn false;\n}\n\nconst results = { variant: multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\" };\n\ntry {\n\t// The trust prompt is about the temp dir this script just created.\n\tif (\n\t\tawait waitFor(\n\t\t\t(t) => /Is this a project you created or one you trust/i.test(t),\n\t\t\t\"trust prompt\",\n\t\t\t30_000,\n\t\t)\n\t) {\n\t\tpty.write(\"1\");\n\t\tawait sleep(2_000);\n\t\tresults.trustAccepted = true;\n\t}\n\n\tconst ready = await waitFor(\n\t\t(t) => /shortcuts|Welcome to Claude Code|Tips for getting started/i.test(t),\n\t\t\"composer ready\",\n\t\t45_000,\n\t);\n\tresults.ready = ready;\n\tif (!ready) throw new Error(\"never reached the composer\");\n\n\tpty.write(ask);\n\tawait sleep(1_200);\n\tpty.write(\"\\r\");\n\n\tconst sawPicker = await waitFor(\n\t\t(t) => /1\\.\\s*Yes/.test(t) && /2\\.\\s*Skip/.test(t),\n\t\t\"picker rows 1. Yes / 2. Skip\",\n\t\t180_000,\n\t);\n\tresults.sawPicker = sawPicker;\n\n\tif (sawPicker) {\n\t\tconst text = screen();\n\t\tfs.writeFileSync(\n\t\t\tpath.join(outDir, `pty-picker-${multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\"}.txt`),\n\t\t\ttext,\n\t\t\t\"utf8\",\n\t\t);\n\t\tconst rows = text\n\t\t\t.split(\"\\n\")\n\t\t\t.map((line, index) => ({ index, line: line.trimEnd() }))\n\t\t\t.filter((row) => /^[^0-9A-Za-z]*[1-9]\\.\\s\\S/.test(row.line));\n\t\tresults.numberedRows = rows.map((row) => `${row.index}: ${row.line.trim()}`);\n\t\tresults.freeTextExactSingle = /3\\.\\s+Type something\\./.test(text);\n\t\tresults.freeTextNoPeriod = /3\\.\\s+Type something(?!\\.)/.test(text);\n\t\tresults.anyFreeTextRow = /Type something/.test(text);\n\t\tresults.chatRow = /Chat about this/.test(text);\n\n\t\tif (!multi && results.anyFreeTextRow === true) {\n\t\t\tpty.write(\"3\");\n\t\t\tresults.digitOpensEditor = await waitFor(\n\t\t\t\t(t) => /Type something…/.test(t) || /Type something\\u2026/.test(t),\n\t\t\t\t\"inline editor placeholder after digit 3\",\n\t\t\t\t20_000,\n\t\t\t);\n\t\t\tfs.writeFileSync(\n\t\t\t\tpath.join(outDir, \"pty-editor-single.txt\"),\n\t\t\t\tscreen(),\n\t\t\t\t\"utf8\",\n\t\t\t);\n\t\t\tpty.write(\"\\x1b\");\n\t\t\tawait sleep(1_000);\n\t\t\tresults.pickerBackAfterEsc = /1\\.\\s*Yes/.test(screen());\n\t\t}\n\t} else {\n\t\tfs.writeFileSync(\n\t\t\tpath.join(outDir, `pty-nopicker-${multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\"}.txt`),\n\t\t\tscreen(),\n\t\t\t\"utf8\",\n\t\t);\n\t}\n} catch (error) {\n\tresults.error = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n\tresults.exited = exited;\n\tfs.writeFileSync(\n\t\tpath.join(outDir, `pty-fail-${multi ? \"multi\" : \"single\"}.txt`),\n\t\tscreen(),\n\t\t\"utf8\",\n\t);\n} finally {\n\ttry {\n\t\tpty.write(\"\\x1b\");\n\t\tpty.write(\"\\x03\");\n\t\tpty.write(\"\\x03\");\n\t} catch {}\n\tawait sleep(800);\n\ttry {\n\t\tpty.kill();\n\t} catch {}\n}\n\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));\nprocess.exit(0);\n","numLines":185,"startLine":1,"totalLines":185}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6adda854-f7cd-4ab7-b042-2050a57f0ed1","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:17:13.723Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"byte-contract\">\nRoot cause traced. One-question freetext encodes 3 discrete frames: [digit N+1, body, CR] (`keystrokes.ts:1206-1249`). Current `injectSequence` sends each immediately after daemon `input-ok` (`answer.ts:1374-1452`). But daemon ACK is emitted synchronously as soon as `session.pty.write(Buffer)` returns (`pty-daemon/.../handlers.ts:120-133`); this proves OS/PTY acceptance, NOT that Claude consumed the digit and switched into inline-editor state. The user's ledger resolved all 3 frames in 5 ms, so body+CR can arrive before the TUI processes the editor-open digit; this exactly permits confirmed PTY writes while the picker remains open. Strong historical evidence: guarded code before commit 498be7a43 explicitly waited for screen advance between frames (25ms polling, up to 1s) and documented that this proved TUI consumption. 498be7a43 removed both guards AND that pacing as if it were only a veto, leaving no consumption barrier. 2.1.228 changelog contains no picker input contract change; version drift is less likely than this deterministic race.\nPrecise live proof: fresh innocuous one-question freetext pickers, drive identical [open, fixed body, CR] at controlled inter-frame delays: 0 ms, 25, 50, 100, 250 ms, at least 3 runs each. Observe only picker-open boolean / tool_result-present boolean and no content. Expect 0ms failure and delayed success threshold. Better production design: retain zero screen/transcript vetoes, but add a non-vetoing deterministic inter-frame pacing delay after every nonfinal frame (start conservatively 100ms, live-prove minimum), independent of renderer/display/lock. ACK stays the write/durability criterion; pacing is sequencing, never confirmation. Stronger but larger option: daemon `input-drain` cannot prove app consumption either, so no need. Also v2 whole-sequence blob is inherently race-prone for multi-frame answers and should remain unconfirmed but still needs paced protocol support or documented limitation.\n</agent-message>"}
