{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:34:03.030Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"targeting-trace\">\nTrace result: stale/wrong PTY targeting is REFUTED for this incident. The audit opaque terminal handle resolves to host terminal f689...; host.db binds that exact terminal to Claude session 41b65f55... and the fork workspace. The questionId cryptographically matches AskUser tool_use call_9uZ... in that same session (capture askedAt +248ms). Phone intake was 02:27:05.718Z; that exact AskUser tool_result appeared at 02:27:06.059Z—341ms later. So the phone bytes were consumed by the intended picker; the user's observed still-open question was a stale visible terminal frame/repaint, not a failed answer or wrong PTY. Production prematurely calls questions.resolve/retract at PTY ack (~5ms) in answer.ts:1083-1143, before semantic tool_result; the later PostToolUse resolve then finds no pending record (question-store.ts:1876-1888,1907-1910). Safest no-barrier fix: keep response/ledger confirmed semantics exactly as required (daemon ack + durable readback), but DO NOT settle/retract QuestionStore on ack. Let positive PostToolUse/transcript settlement (question-store.ts:1960-2074) retire it; optionally retain remote provenance from the confirmed ledger. Add a non-vetoing post-write repaint nudge to the session (terminal.ts already has nudgeRepaint at 1374-1393) so the renderer visibly catches up; failure to repaint must never downgrade/refuse. Tests: (1) ack-confirmed answer remains pending until PostToolUse; (2) positive tool_result settles/retracts with phone provenance; (3) missing/unreadable transcript stays discoverable but answer response remains confirmed; (4) repaint nudge called after confirmed and failures swallowed/logged; (5) real desktop CDP/UI evidence: phone answer yields tool_result then visible picker disappears, including renderer disconnect/reconnect. Generic stale path review: capture validates active host row, stores exact hostTerminalId/workspace; prepare/adopt requires the same daemon session ID and workspace, and final check keys by same hostTerminalId. No cross-terminal mapping path found. Also notifications.ts:160-176 comments are stale (still claim guards prevent forged capture) and should be corrected.\n</agent-message>"}
