{"parentUuid":"c9841cfe-0158-4dd2-8cb5-bc3077128b17","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Verify installed desktop build","description":"Confirmed installed Superset 1.20.0 from executable and uninstall metadata, running app process tree, visible nonblank renderer, and digest-verified installer/build mapping to the final shipped build. Packaged metadata does not independently expose the commit SHA.","activeForm":"Verifying installed desktop build","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Inspect companion runtime","description":"Confirmed installed host-service and PTY daemon are running from app.asar; daemon v0.4.0 manifest advertises protocol v3. Current restart logs contain no answer attempts or guard failures yet. Detected installed Claude CLI 2.1.228 versus byte contract proven on 2.1.226, requiring live answer E2E.","activeForm":"Inspecting companion runtime","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Run closed-loop emulator E2E","description":"Completed live post-restart companion E2E on Claude CLI 2.1.228. A real physical-phone free-text request was durably confirmed in 5 ms with null failure and empty guards; a separate safe emulator single-select request also durably confirmed with protocol-v3 daemon active. The scratch status parser expected the old response shape, but ledger proof confirmed success.","activeForm":"Running closed-loop emulator E2E","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Test availability boundaries","description":"Verified renderer-visible/nonblank post-restart state and proved live phone free-text bytes reached protocol-v3 PTY and durable ledger with no guards. A genuine display-off/Windows-lock test is not currently executable: Windows automation cannot cross the lock screen and no phone/watch is connected via ADB. This limitation is reported explicitly rather than treating headless architecture as E2E proof.","activeForm":"Testing availability boundaries","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Eliminate emulator identity interference","description":"Blocked safely: creating a distinct emulator identity through the real pairing flow would currently persist the secret-bearing QR URI in host-service.log. Manual DB/key insertion would bypass pairing. No existing device state changed. Production logging fix is task #6; emulator identity creation must wait for that shipped fix.","activeForm":"Eliminating emulator identity interference","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Remove secret-bearing pairing log","description":"Security issue confirmed, but defer implementation until the user's reported answer-consumption failure is root-caused. The immediate priority is proving why protocol-v3 PTY acceptance did not dismiss the live Claude 2.1.228 question.","activeForm":"Removing secret-bearing pairing log","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"Prove PTY consumption failure","description":"Incident proven end-to-end from safe metadata: the phone answer targeted the exact Claude session/picker; matching AskUser tool_result appeared 341 ms after phone intake. The answer did work, but the visible terminal failed to repaint, leaving a stale picker frame. Root cause is premature QuestionStore resolve/retract at 5 ms PTY acknowledgment plus no non-vetoing repaint nudge. Fix should preserve confirmed semantics, defer question settlement to positive PostToolUse/tool_result, and nudge repaint best-effort without becoming a barrier.","activeForm":"Proving PTY consumption failure","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"8","subject":"Fix stale picker settlement","description":"Preserve guardless confirmed write semantics, stop resolving/retracting pending questions at PTY acknowledgment, settle only through positive PostToolUse/tool_result evidence, and issue a non-vetoing repaint nudge after confirmed writes so the visible picker disappears.","activeForm":"Fixing stale picker settlement","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":8},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8ec3541a-e661-47fd-aa83-50c9ff52995a","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:49:08.635Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\installed-asar-check","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
