{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:50:38.095Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8d5e3bb38fc80d24</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_rLdoDzT07ufaUbcfwvRbpOlz</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a8d5e3bb38fc80d24.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review answer fence changes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Review complete. Diff isolated (primary HEAD == worktree HEAD 25fcc9e93; compared trees directly, CRLF-noise filtered): `FEATURES.md` + 6 host-service production files + 2 test files.\n\n---\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\index.ts:1948\nDefect: `nudgeRepaint: nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint` wires an impl that destructures `{terminalId, workspaceId}` (terminal.ts:1415-1420), but the only call site passes a `HostTerminalRef` — keys `hostTerminalId`/`hostWorkspaceId` (answer.ts:957-960, called at answer.ts:1164).\nFailure: Every confirmed companion answer calls `writableSession(undefined, undefined)` → `{error: \"Terminal session not found\"}` → repaint NEVER happens in production; only `companion.answer.repaint_failed` log lines. The entire repaint half of this diff is dead on arrival, and the FEATURES.md claim (\"a best-effort PTY resize nudge asks Claude to repaint its consumed picker\") ships false. Tests pass because `answerHarness` uses a fake repaint that accepts `HostTerminalRef` (answer-guardless.test.ts:229, expects `[HOST]` = `{hostTerminalId, hostWorkspaceId}`), never the real adapter. Also a TS2322 at index.ts:1948, which only the absent type gate hides.\nFix: Adapt at the wiring site: `nudgeRepaint: ({hostTerminalId, hostWorkspaceId}) =&gt; nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint({terminalId: hostTerminalId, workspaceId: hostWorkspaceId})`.\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts:752 (+ answer.ts:779)\nDefect: The fence counts `in_flight` rows of OTHER live requests, but `claimForAnswer` (attempt-ledger.ts:648) claims `in_flight` keyed on requestId only, BEFORE the lease/lock — so a concurrent request's pre-write claim reads as \"already delivered\".\nFailure: Phone and watch answer the same question near-simultaneously (the exact first-answer-wins scenario). Both claim `in_flight` (answer.ts:845). B then sits in the `await writer.prepare(...)` daemon round-trip (answer.ts:969) holding an `in_flight` row the whole time. A wins the lease, enters the lock, and `findQuestionFence` at answer.ts:779 sees B's row → A is refused 409 \"an answer for this question was already delivered … it will not be typed again\" though ZERO keystrokes were written by anyone. If B's fence read then beats A's outer-catch flip to `failed` (answer.ts:1322), B is refused too: two devices, both told \"already delivered\", nothing typed, question still pending. This violates the stated requirement — a pre-write claim is neither a durable duplicate nor an ambiguous write. Note `in_flight` inclusion IS load-bearing for the post-injection/pre-`recordOutcome` window (recordOutcome runs outside the lock at answer.ts:1120), so it cannot simply be dropped.\nFix: Split the states: claim as `claimed`, promote to `in_flight` durably INSIDE the lock immediately before the first keystroke; fence on `in_flight`/`confirmed`/`unconfirmed` only. Crash pre-write leaves non-fencing `claimed`; crash mid-type still fences.\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts:759\nDefect: `findQuestionFence` throws a plain `Error` on an unvalidatable candidate row; thrown inside the lock pre-write, it hits the non-SealedError catch (answer.ts:1290) which durably records THIS request as `unconfirmed` — a fence status — though nothing was written.\nFailure: One corrupt/foreign/schema-drifted row with a fence status on question Q (e.g., a newer build's row this build's `validate` rejects) → every fresh answer request for Q not only 500s but each mints a NEW never-pruned `unconfirmed` row claiming \"may have been typed\". Even after the corruption is repaired, Q stays permanently fenced by rows that provably wrote zero bytes — a durable false ambiguous-write fence, and a direct violation of the \"corrupt row costs one requestId its status\" containment rule in FEATURES.md.\nFix: Throw a `sealed(503, \"internal\", \"nothing was written …\")` (or convert to sealed before the lock callback returns) so the outer catch records `failed`, which is not in the fence set.\n\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-store.ts:1967 (called from answer.ts:1156)\nDefect: `markRemoteAnswered` throws on an unknown questionId, and it runs after two `await`s (recordOutcome, audit append) during which the record can leave the store.\nFailure: Question asked &gt;24 h ago (settledAt falls back to `askedAtMs`, question-store.ts:1613), companion answer confirmed, a racing capture supersedes it stale and a `prune()` deletes it before answer.ts:1156 runs → throw → device receives an internal error and an `unconfirmed` audit line for an answer that is durably `confirmed` (row itself is safe; `recordOutcome` no-ops on non-in_flight). Retry then correctly gets the 409 fence.\nFix: Make `markRemoteAnswered` return false on unknown ids (mirror `markStale`'s tolerance) or wrap the call in the same log-only handling as the repaint.\n\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:788-792\nDefect: The fence 409 hardcodes `outcome: \"answered\"` and message \"was already delivered\", but the fence row may be `unconfirmed` (partial/unknown write) or a live `in_flight`, and after a restart `resolvedBy` is null and `resolvedAtMs` null for non-confirmed rows.\nFailure: A phone polling after an `unconfirmed` whole-sequence failure sees a later fresh request answered with `outcome: \"answered\"` — overclaiming certainty the v2-daemon `unconfirmed` contract deliberately refuses elsewhere.\nFix: Derive the detail from `durableFence.status` (answered vs may-have-been-delivered) instead of a constant.\n\nChecked and clean: secret pairing log fix (QR URI removed from logs; `pairingRef` exists at pairing.ts:238 and is genuinely non-secret; FEATURES.md text updated with markers intact); notifications.ts (comment-only); PostToolUse-before-provenance race (handled bidirectionally — `resolve` inherits `remoteAnswerBy` at question-store.ts:1958-1959, `markRemoteAnswered` back-stamps a resolved record at 1974-1977, both orders tested); stale-picker settlement (confirmed answers stay pending until exact-toolUseId PostToolUse/transcript settlement; supersede path at question-store.ts:1852-1877 intact); fresh-request fence excludes `failed`/`closed_not_received` so clean failures stay answerable; crash-mid-type and crash-post-ack both leave a durable fence and post-restart the question is unknown (no retype path); `assertAnswerDeps` wired at the sole composition root (index.ts:814).\n\n**FIX-FIRST**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>138969</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>57</tool_uses><duration_ms>814067</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
