rget input.\n189-\t */\n190-\twriteInput: RawWriteFn;\n191-\t/**\n192:\t * Best-effort repaint after an acknowledged answer. This asks the running TUI\n193-\t * to redraw from its own state; it is never an answer precondition or outcome\n194-\t * check, and failure may only be logged.\n195-\t */\n196-\tnudgeRepaint(input: HostTerminalRef): { success: true } | { error: string };\n197-\t/**\n198-\t * Paste-framed write, for `/v1/message` ONLY. Deliberately a different shape\n199-\t * (async, `{text, submit}`) so it cannot be swapped with `writeInput`. Never\n200-\t * reachable from the injector.\n201-\t *\n202-\t * `terminalId` / `workspaceId` are HOST.DB ids from `resolveHostTerminal`, not\n203-\t * wire handles — the field names are the pty writer's, and the writer looks\n204-\t * them up in its live session map.\n205-\t *\n206-\t * NOTE, because the header comment on `handleMessage` used to get this wrong:\n207-\t * `submit: true` appends `\\r` OUTSIDE the bracketed-paste frame. The body is\n208-\t * inert against a picker; that `\\r` is not. (MESSAGE-ECHO) is why the message\n--\n565-// incoherent record quarantined every other record's 24 hours — rows validate\n566-// individually now, so a corrupt row costs exactly one requestId its status.\n567-//\n568-\\ The message path keeps its own small in-memory store below: a message has no\n569-// question and no lease, and it makes no coverage claim, so it needs none of this.\n570-\n571-/**\n572- * §7.5 — the message path's own idempotency record. Kept separate from\n573- * `AnswerAttemptRecord` rather than folded into it: a message has no question\n574- * and no lease, and inventing empty values for those would put fiction into the\n575- * audit trail the residual race (§11.7) depends on.\n576- */\n577-export interface MessageAttemptRecord {\n578-\trequestId: RequestId;\n579-\tterminalId: TerminalId;\n580-\tstartedAtMs: EpochMs;\n581:\tstatus: \"sent\" | \"unconfirmed\" | \"failed\";\n582-\tsentAtMs: EpochMs | null;\n