ilures don't first write unconfirmed. Add tests with throwing beginWrite/non-Sealed pre-write fault proving fresh request can retry/type; preserve ambiguous post-promotion behavior. 2) PostToolUse-before-mark remote provenance: actual createNotifyingCaptureSink can publish desktop question.resolved before answer marks remote provenance; late mark currently mutates only memory. Implement a corrective or deferred event mechanism so connected clients ultimately receive exact phone/watch provenance, without delaying/vetoing answer writes or settlement. Test through the notifying sink/event publisher race, not bare store mutation. No answer barriers. Keep wire status union four statuses. Run focused/full companion tests, scoped Biome, REFERR relevant. Do not commit. Report exact behavior/files.","outputFile":"C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a98ebbe975bf745f7.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20d60b5c-d894-4602-a6b6-74b19b436ced","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T13:34:11.907Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a152ef71bff9acfbd</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a152ef71bff9acfbd.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify revised answer changes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Review target: the \"uncommitted diff\" no longer exists uncommitted — it was committed in the shared checkout as `408ecc9c5` (settle companion answers after Claude consumes them) + `5bc2dd144` (keep claimed status internal) minutes before this review. Shared working tree verified byte-identical (CRLF-normalized) to clean HEAD `5bc2dd144`; reviewed that two-commit range. Verification run: `attempt-ledger.test.ts` 4/4, `question-lifecycle.test.ts` + `answer-guardless.test.ts` 38/38 pass; Biome clean on all 10 touched files; feature-marker gate green (147/147); no CHECK constraint on `answer_attempts.status`, so the new `claimed` enum value needs no migration.\n\n```\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1308 (and :1344-1349)\nDefect: Both catch paths settle a provably pre-write failure — the ledger row still `claimed`, meaning zero bytes could have been written — as `unconfirmed`, and `unconfirmed` is in QUESTION_FENCE_STATUSES, so the live question is permanently fenced.\nFailure: A non-SealedError escapes before beginWrite promotion — e.g. `encodeAnswer` rethrows a non-KeystrokeEncodingError at answer.ts:933 (a branch the code explicitly anticipates), or `locks.runExclusive` infrastructure fails before the lock body runs. Outer catch at :1341 sees `durableStatus === \"claimed\"` (proof nothing was typed) yet the non-sealed arm at :1349 records `unconfirmed`. Every subsequent fresh request for that question then hits the beginWrite fence and gets 409 \"an answer for this question may already have been delivered; it will not be typed again\" — false, nothing was ever typed. Restart does not heal it: rehydration converts `claimed`→`failed` and `in_flight`→`unconfirmed`, never `unconfirmed`→anything. The question is unanswerable from phone/watch forever; the agent stays blocked until the desktop is touched — the exact scenario the companion exists for. The inner catch at :1308 has the same defect (records `unconfirmed` without checking the row is still `claimed`); the module's own header (\"pre-write claims … provably wrote nothing and no longer fence their questions\") states the invariant these two sites violate.\nFix: In both catch sites, read the ledger status first: if still `claimed`, record `failed` (failureCode `internal`) — zero-write is proven by the un-promoted status; reserve `unconfirmed` for rows already promoted to `in_flight`.\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1352\nDefect: The outer-catch recordOutcome passes `leaseId: null`, and ledger recordOutcome unconditionally overwrites the column — so an `in_flight` row whose leaseId was just filled by beginWrite promotion loses it when a post-promotion error settles the row as unconfirmed.\nFailure: Error thrown after beginWrite but outside the inner try (rare) or replayed via the outer catch: the durable unconfirmed row that fences the question forever carries `leaseId: null`, erasing which lease held the terminal when bytes may have landed — the one forensic datum the promotion step was added to preserve.\nFix: Preserve the existing leaseId on catch-path settlement (omit the column from the update, or read-then-write it).\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1347\nDefect: `error.body.code as AttemptFailureCode` is an unchecked cast; SealedErrorCode additionally contains `session_expired` and `access_denied`, which LEDGER_FAILURE_CODES/validate() reject.\nFailure: Pre-existing cast, but the new `claimed` branch widens when it executes (now covers every sealed throw between claim at :829 and the lock). If any future sealed throw in that span uses `session_expired`/`access_denied`, the written row fails validate() on every later read: claimForAnswer replay throws \"occupied by a row this build cannot validate\" and status reads break — the requestId row is poisoned durably.\nFix: Narrow the code through a runtime membership check against LEDGER_FAILURE_CODES, falling back to `internal`.\n```\n\nChecked clean: claim→beginWrite arbitration (claimed excluded from fence, promotion transactional and terminal-lock-serialized, lease double-protects same-question races; concurrency tests exercise real SQL); fresh-request fencing (loser rows settle `failed` = non-fencing, fence 409 correct for confirmed/unconfirmed, `closed_not_received` tombstone semantics untouched); status readback (`claimed` mapped to wire `in_flight`, never leaks — commit 5bc2dd144's types.ts change matches toWireOutcome); restart rehydration (claimed→failed ordering and validate() invariants, including failed-with-null-resolvedAtMs); settlement/provenance (markRemoteAnswered pending-until-PostToolUse, both race directions tested and deliberate, no double-onSettled); repaint wiring (nudgeRepaint mandatory in assertAnswerDeps with the only production AnswerDeps site wired in index.ts:1948, failure log-only and post-confirmation, resizeGeneration guard sound under overlapping nudges); pairing redaction (qrUri removed from host-service log, `pairingRef` is the non-secret pid, authenticated tRPC route companion.ts:333 still returns qrUri to the desktop dialog so pairing is not bricked); notifications.ts (comment-only); FEATURES.md markers.\n\n**FIX-FIRST**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>110543</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>792965</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
