tly anticipates), or `locks.runExclusive` infrastructure fails before the lock body runs. Outer catch at :1341 sees `durableStatus === \"claimed\"` (proof nothing was typed) yet the non-sealed arm at :1349 records `unconfirmed`. Every subsequent fresh request for that question then hits the beginWrite fence and gets 409 \"an answer for this question may already have been delivered; it will not be typed again\" — false, nothing was ever typed. Restart does not heal it: rehydration converts `claimed`→`failed` and `in_flight`→`unconfirmed`, never `unconfirmed`→anything. The question is unanswerable from phone/watch forever; the agent stays blocked until the desktop is touched — the exact scenario the companion exists for. The inner catch at :1308 has the same defect (records `unconfirmed` without checking the row is still `claimed`); the module's own header (\"pre-write claims … provably wrote nothing and no longer fence their questions\") states the invariant these two sites violate.\nFix: In both catch sites, read the ledger status first: if still `claimed`, record `failed` (failureCode `internal`) — zero-write is proven by the un-promoted status; reserve `unconfirmed` for rows already promoted to `in_flight`.\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1352\nDefect: The outer-catch recordOutcome passes `leaseId: null`, and ledger recordOutcome unconditionally overwrites the column — so an `in_flight` row whose leaseId was just filled by beginWrite promotion loses it when a post-promotion error settles the row as unconfirmed.\nFailure: Error thrown after beginWrite but outside the inner try (rare) or replayed via the outer catch: the durable unconfirmed row that fences the question forever carries `leaseId: null`, erasing which lease held the terminal when bytes may have landed — the one forensic datum the promotion step was added to preserve.\nFix: Preserve the existing leaseId on catch-path settlement (omit the column from the update, or read-then-write it).\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1347\nDefect: `error.body.code as AttemptFailureCode` is an unchecked cast; SealedErrorCode additionally contains `session_expired` and `access_denied`, which LEDGER_FAILURE_CODES/validate() reject.\nFailure: Pre-existing cast, but the new `claimed` branch widens when it executes (now covers every sealed throw between claim at :829 and the lock). If any future sealed throw in that span uses `session_expired`/`access_denied`, the written row fails validate() on every later read: claimForAnswer replay throws \"occupied by a row this build cannot validate\" and status reads break — the requestId row is poisoned durably.\nFix: Narrow the code through a runtime membership check against LEDGER_FAILURE_CODES, falling back to `internal`.\n```\n\nChecked clean: claim→beginWrite arbitration (claimed excluded from fence, promotion transactional and terminal-lock-serialized, lease double-protects same-question races; concurrency tests exercise real SQL); fresh-request fencing (loser rows settle `failed` = non-fencing, fence 409 correct for confirmed/unconfirmed, `closed_not_received` tombstone semantics untouched); status readback (`claimed` mapped to wire `in_flight`, never leaks — commit 5bc2dd144's types.ts change matches toWireOutcome); restart rehydration (claimed→failed ordering and validate() invariants, including failed-with-null-resolvedAtMs); settlement/provenance (markRemoteAnswered pending-until-PostToolUse, both race directions tested and deliberate, no double-onSettled); repaint wiring (nudgeRepaint mandatory in assertAnswerDeps with the only production AnswerDeps site wired in index.ts:1948, failure log-only and post-confirmation, resizeGeneration guard sound under overlapping nudges); pairing redaction (qrUri removed from host-service log, `pairingRe