2-liner.\n\n2. `packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts:1460-1468` — third hand-built `question.resolved` frame literal, byte-identical in shape to `:1515-1522` (and a near-twin at `:724-731` with `outcome: \"unknown\"`). Cost: a `types.ts:1182` frame-shape change now needs 3 coordinated edits, and 2 of the 3 already differ in error discipline. Reuse: add a `publishQuestionResolved(deps, {...})` sibling to the existing `publishPendingQuestion` (`index.ts:1781`), which already owns the try/catch + \"phone falls back to counts\" log convention — the new function has neither, so it is the only one of the three that can throw into its caller.\n\n3. `packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts:1448` — `resolvedBy: NonNullable&lt;PendingQuestion[\"resolvedBy\"]&gt;` restates the exported `ResolvedBy` (`types.ts:737`; `PendingQuestion.resolvedBy` is literally `ResolvedBy | null` at `:779`). The other side of the same seam already imports `ResolvedBy` (`answer.ts:246`). Cost: two spellings of one type across one call, so a grep for `ResolvedBy` users misses this signature.\n\n4. `packages/host-service/src/companion/answer.ts:1320-1323` vs `:1355-1370` — the same \"durable status `claimed` → `failed`/`internal`, else `unconfirmed`/`null`\" rule stated twice, 35 lines apart, in two different idioms: an `outcome` object literal in the inner catch, split `preWrite ?` ternaries in the outer. Cost: the pre-write fencing rule is the diff's core semantic and it has no single home; changing it requires finding both spellings, and they can silently diverge (the outer one additionally folds in `SealedError`). Reuse: extract one `durableFailureOutcome(durable, error): { status, failureCode }` and have both catches spread it.\n\n5. `packages/host-service/src/companion/answer-guardless.test.ts:393` — `harness.deps.locks.runExclusive = createTerminalLockRegistry().runExclusive` allocates a whole second registry just to steal a method. `runExclusive` closes over that registry's own `