/src/companion/answer-guardless.test.ts:254` and `:393` — monkey-patches a live registry instead of injecting a double.**\n`locks.runExclusive = options.lockRun`, then mid-test restore from a throwaway `createTerminalLockRegistry()`. Cost: the harness depends on the registry returning a writable-method object; if `createTerminalLockRegistry` ever returns a frozen object or class instance, both the setup and the restore break obscurely. Restore is also a second site that must know a swap happened — drop it and the \"retry succeeds\" assertion becomes vacuous.\n\n## Correct altitude (no change wanted)\n\n- `RemoteAnswerPublisherDeps` (`index.ts:1504`) as its own interface rather than `Pick&lt;NotifyingSinkDeps,…&gt;` — matches the documented `CurationGateDeps` precedent at `index.ts:1424`.\n- `publishQuestionResolved` (`index.ts:1429`) now backs all three publish sites (`:724`, `:1494`, `:1531`); the wire shape lives in one place.\n- Injecting the publisher into `AnswerDeps` rather than importing `EventStreamServer` into `answer.ts` keeps `answer.ts` as pure policy and `index.ts` as the composition root.\n- `toLedgerFailureCode`/`isLedgerFailureCode` placement — validation at the boundary that defines the accepted set, reused by row validation.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>80175</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>18</tool_uses><duration_ms>223024</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
