{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T16:58:52.911Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a19fd835c373088c4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a19fd835c373088c4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace latest partial answer\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Root cause confirmed\n\nThe phone correctly submitted **all four answers**. The desktop then sent the correct five-key sequence:\n\n1. Question 1 selection  \n2. Question 2 selection  \n3. Question 3 selection  \n4. Question 4 selection  \n5. Final review-screen Enter  \n\nThe failure is in **sequencing**, not the phone, targeting, lock screen, or answer encoding.\n\n- The bridge sent those five frames consecutively.\n- The PTY daemon acknowledged each frame immediately after `pty.write()` returned: `packages/pty-daemon/src/handlers/handlers.ts:120-133`.\n- That acknowledgment only means **Windows accepted the bytes into the PTY**. It does **not** mean Claude consumed the key and advanced to the next question.\n- The entire four-answer request was marked `confirmed` in only **82 ms**.\n- The untouched picker advanced from question 1 to question 2, proving only the first selection reached the intended picker state. Frames 2–5 arrived before Claude finished transitioning and were ignored or consumed in the wrong state.\n- No completed AskUser tool result followed.\n\nThe problematic assumption is explicit in the injector: it sends another frame immediately after each PTY acknowledgment and declares success after all writes: `packages/host-service/src/companion/answer.ts:1440-1518`.\n\nThis was **not caused by Windows being locked**. The logs show the request arrived while locked, and question 1 still worked. It was also **not a malformed phone request**: intake recorded four valid `select` answers.\n\n### Important build distinction\n\nThe currently installed `7e0d25f3c` build additionally retracted the phone question immediately after those PTY acknowledgments, falsely presenting the whole sequence as delivered.\n\nThe published but uninstalled `4a9978200` build fixes that premature settlement/retraction behavior, but it still uses the same immediate frame loop. Therefore, **installing `4a9978200` alone will not fix this four-question race**.\n\nA further code fix is required: pace each question-changing frame until Claude has had time to consume the transition, without making renderer, screen, transcript, or Windows lock state into a veto.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>49</tool_uses><duration_ms>1160524</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
