{"parentUuid":"b01be8b9-6c52-4461-aca2-21e3619e3019","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3fbc42925ded49f9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a3fbc42925ded49f9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Prove four-question pacing\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Pacing proof completed and reported to the coordinator.\n\n- **Burst input failed 2/2** on real Claude Code 2.1.228.\n- Fixed **100, 250, 500, and 1000 ms** gaps each succeeded in the current trials with an exact four-answer `tool_result`.\n- **500 ms** is the recommended conservative deterministic inter-frame delay.\n- The delay must remain independent of screen, renderer, transcript, and Windows session state.\n- T3 Code offers no PTY pacing precedent; it answers questions atomically through the Claude Agent SDK.\n- No production files were changed; the repository remains clean.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>58</tool_uses><duration_ms>934725</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:30:40.279Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d23a590e-88da-418e-8549-0e8bfcafaba1","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:30:40.279Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
