, deadline/lease failure. Run focused bun tests + scoped Biome. Do not commit/push or invoke skills. Report files and tests.","result":"","isRawTranscript":true}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a4dbf3c8-a425-4367-b297-78bd218caf23","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:36:22.584Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>abf1b7580f62d386a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\abf1b7580f62d386a.output</output-file>\n<status>killed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Analyze multi-question byte race\" was stopped by Claude</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The root cause is confirmed: the phone correctly submitted **four single-select answers**, encoded as **five protocol-v3 frames** (four choices plus final Enter). The installed build received PTY acknowledgments for all five and marked the attempt confirmed in **82 ms**.\n\nThose acknowledgments only mean `pty.write()` accepted the bytes—not that Claude consumed each key and advanced its picker. Question 1 advanced; frames 2–5 arrived before the question-2 UI became active and were ignored or applied against the old state. There is no matching AskUser completion.\n\nThe newer uninstalled build fixes settlement honesty and repainting, but **does not fix this inter-question race**. I’m proving the pacing boundary with a controlled four-question test, then I’ll add non-vetoing transition pacing that works with the renderer absent, screen off, or Windows locked.</result>\n</task-notification>"}
