{"parentUuid":"5fddeff7-7fcb-49bc-8316-17617fa1e13e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_00d8cf41dd15c00f016a7caf30d27c8191a45ad19b2689fdc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6682,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":53760,"output_tokens":127,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_RIKVr4evWzWYcsEFGesHhKdH","name":"Grep","input":{"path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts","pattern":"injectSequence|wait:|effective|INTER_KEYSTROKE","output_mode":"content","-n":true,"context":8,"head_limit":160}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8ef68701-cd7f-47fd-b23a-9bb7018a9341","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:36:51.714Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"8ef68701-cd7f-47fd-b23a-9bb7018a9341","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5548f27b-2b1d-4e0e-84da-bd27822c3dc9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_RIKVr4evWzWYcsEFGesHhKdH","type":"tool_result","content":"1-/**\n2- * (COMPANION-BRIDGE) — answer injection and idempotency (§11).\n3- *\n4- * (ANSWER-GUARDLESS) A pending, captured Claude question is directly answerable\n5- * from a paired phone or watch. After the request boundary validates question\n6- * identity and answer shape, `encodeAnswer` produces the proven byte sequence and\n7: * `injectSequence` writes it to the captured terminal under the per-terminal lock.\n8- * No transcript, screen, renderer, Windows interactive-session, agent-binding,\n9- * permission-latch or marker observation may veto or downgrade that write.\n10- *\n11- * The lock, answer-wide lease and durable request ledger remain: they prevent two\n12- * devices from interleaving bytes and make retries idempotent. Each PTY write is\n13- * counted only after the daemon acknowledges `pty.write`, consecutive discrete\n14- * keystrokes are separated by a deterministic, state-blind pacing delay\n15: * (`INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS` — it reads nothing and can never veto), and the\n16- * response is confirmed only after the ledger outcome is written and read back.\n17- * An actual PTY failure prevents confirmation; a ledger failure after landed\n18- * bytes returns an honest, duplicate-fenced `unconfirmed` outcome.\n19- *\n20- * Answer attempts record empty guard arrays and `null` evaluation solely for\n21- * persisted audit-schema compatibility.\n22- */\n23-\n--\n82- */\n83-export const LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000;\n84-\n85-/** Poll interval while waiting for the emulator mirror to reflect our last byte. */\n86-export const SCREEN_ADVANCE_POLL_MS = 25;\n87-\n88-/**\n89- * Hard ceiling on one keystroke sequence's WRITE work, excluding pacing. The\n90: * effective deadline in `injectSequence` adds the sequence's own deterministic\n91: * pacing budget (`INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS` per inter-keystroke gap): the\n92- * longest LEGAL prompt — `MAX_QUESTIONS_PER_PROMPT` (32) questions, each at\n93- * worst nine digit-addressable toggles plus the advance arrow, plus the\n94- * review-screen return — encodes to 321 keystrokes, whose 320 paced gaps alone\n95- * are 160 s, so a fixed total would silently abort every such sequence\n96- * mid-prompt. Bounds how long the terminal lock can be held; the answer lease\n97- * is re-extended immediately before every write, so its TTL only has to cover\n98- * one gap plus one write, never the whole sequence.\n99- */\n--\n110- *\n111- * This is PACING, not a guard: it consults no screen, transcript, renderer,\n112- * session or lock state, it runs unconditionally after every non-final\n113- * acknowledged discrete keystroke, and it can never veto or downgrade a write.\n114- * The legacy protocol-v2 path is untouched — it queues the ENTIRE sequence as\n115- * one ordered frame, has no per-keystroke acknowledgement to pace, and keeps\n116- * its honest whole-sequence `unconfirmed` outcome.\n117- */\n118:export const INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS = 500;\n119-\n120-/** PROTOCOL §7.5 — a message body is 1..8 192 chars. */\n121-export const MESSAGE_MAX_CHARS = 8_192;\n122-\n123-/**\n124- * (MESSAGE-ECHO) How long `/v1/message` waits for the composer to render the\n125- * text it just pasted, before it will write the trailing submit.\n126- *\n--\n1160-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n1161-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedBy: null,\n1162-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: durableFence.resolvedAtMs,\n1163-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\toutcome:\n1164-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdurableFence.status === \"confirmed\" ? \"answered\" : \"unknown\",\n1165-\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n1166-\t\t\t\t\t\t);\n1167-\t\t\t\t\t}\n1168:\t\t\t\t\treturn injectSequence(deps, {\n1169-\t\t\t\t\t\tquestion,\n1170-\t\t\t\t\t\thost,\n1171-\t\t\t\t\t\tkeystrokes,\n1172-\t\t\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n1173-\t\t\t\t\t\tacknowledgedInputSupported: prepared.acknowledgedInputSupported,\n1174-\t\t\t\t\t\twriter,\n1175-\t\t\t\t\t});\n1176-\t\t\t\t},\n--\n1439- *\n1440- * PTY input is an ordered byte stream. We therefore write the already-encoded\n1441- * sequence in order and confirm immediately after the daemon acknowledges every\n1442- * `pty.write`. The old mirror-advance wait could downgrade a successful write to\n1443- * `unconfirmed` merely because the renderer had not repainted; that is explicitly\n1444- * not an outcome check.\n1445- *\n1446- * (ANSWER-PACING) Acknowledged discrete keystrokes are separated by a\n1447: * deterministic `INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS` sleep — after every non-final frame,\n1448- * never after the last — because the real CLI consumes back-to-back writes\n1449- * faster than its picker transitions and drops keystrokes. The sleep reads\n1450- * nothing and decides nothing; the lease is re-extended after each sleep,\n1451- * immediately before the next write, and the deadline is widened by exactly the\n1452- * sequence's pacing budget so the longest legal prompt still fits. The legacy\n1453- * one-frame protocol-v2 write is never paced.\n1454- */\n1455:export async function injectSequence(\n1456-\tdeps: AnswerDeps,\n1457-\tinput: {\n1458-\t\tquestion: PendingQuestion;\n1459-\t\thost: HostTerminalRef;\n1460-\t\tkeystrokes: readonly Keystroke[];\n1461-\t\tleaseId: string;\n1462-\t\tacknowledgedInputSupported: boolean;\n1463-\t\twriter: RawPtyWriter;\n--\n1505-\t}\n1506-\n1507-\t\\ (ANSWER-PACING) The deadline bounds the sequence it actually runs: the\n1508-\t// fixed write budget plus THIS sequence's own pacing gaps. Only the\n1509-\t// acknowledged per-keystroke path is paced, so only it earns the extension;\n1510-\t// the legacy single-frame path keeps the bare write budget.\n1511-\tconst pacedGaps = acknowledgedInputSupported ? frames.length - 1 : 0;\n1512-\tconst deadlineMs =\n1513:\t\tdeps.now() + SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS + pacedGaps * INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS;\n1514-\n1515-\tfor (let frameIndex = 0; frameIndex < frames.length; frameIndex += 1) {\n1516-\t\tconst frame = frames[frameIndex];\n1517-\t\tif (frame === undefined) {\n1518-\t\t\treturn abort(\"missing input frame\", frameIndex, \"not_written\");\n1519-\t\t}\n1520-\t\tif (deps.now() >= deadlineMs) {\n1521-\t\t\treturn abort(\"sequence deadline exceeded\", frame.abortAt, \"not_written\");\n--\n1576-\t\t// transition all get the same gap — and never after the final frame.\n1577-\t\t// The lease is re-extended at the top of the next iteration, AFTER this\n1578-\t\t// sleep and immediately before the next write, so a paced gap can never\n1579-\t\t// let a lapsed lease keep typing. A sleep that throws is logged and\n1580-\t\t\\ skipped: pacing improves delivery but must never veto or downgrade\n1581-\t\t// bytes that already landed.\n1582-\t\tif (acknowledgedInputSupported && frameIndex < frames.length - 1) {\n1583-\t\t\ttry {\n1584:\t\t\t\tawait deps.wait(INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS);\n1585-\t\t\t} catch (error) {\n1586-\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n1587-\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.pacing_wait_failed\",\n1588-\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: question.questionId,\n1589-\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n1590-\t\t\t\t\tframeIndex,\n1591-\t\t\t\t\terror: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n1592-\t\t\t\t});"}]},"uuid":"23f14e5f-93ec-4ca4-9fcc-aab36d8dc945","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:36:56.229Z","toolUseResult":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"1-/**\n2- * (COMPANION-BRIDGE) — answer injection and idempotency (§11).\n3- *\n4- * (ANSWER-GUARDLESS) A pending, captured Claude question is directly answerable\n5- * from a paired phone or watch. After the request boundary validates question\n6- * identity and answer shape, `encodeAnswer` produces the proven byte sequence and\n7: * `injectSequence` writes it to the captured terminal under the per-terminal lock.\n8- * No transcript, screen, renderer, Windows interactive-session, agent-binding,\n9- * permission-latch or marker observation may veto or downgrade that write.\n10- *\n11- * The lock, answer-wide lease and durable request ledger remain: they prevent two\n12- * devices from interleaving bytes and make retries idempotent. Each PTY write is\n13- * counted only after the daemon acknowledges `pty.write`, consecutive discrete\n14- * keystrokes are separated by a deterministic, state-blind pacing delay\n15: * (`INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS` — it reads nothing and can never veto), and the\n16- * response is confirmed only after the ledger outcome is written and read back.\n17- * An actual PTY failure prevents confirmation; a ledger failure after landed\n18- * bytes returns an honest, duplicate-fenced `unconfirmed` outcome.\n19- *\n20- * Answer attempts record empty guard arrays and `null` evaluation solely for\n21- * persisted audit-schema compatibility.\n22- */\n23-\n--\n82- */\n83-export const LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000;\n84-\n85-/** Poll interval while waiting for the emulator mirror to reflect our last byte. */\n86-export const SCREEN_ADVANCE_POLL_MS = 25;\n87-\n88-/**\n89- * Hard ceiling on one keystroke sequence's WRITE work, excluding pacing. The\n90: * effective deadline in `injectSequence` adds the sequence's own deterministic\n91: * pacing budget (`INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS` per inter-keystroke gap): the\n92- * longest LEGAL prompt — `MAX_QUESTIONS_PER_PROMPT` (32) questions, each at\n93- * worst nine digit-addressable toggles plus the advance arrow, plus the\n94- * review-screen return — encodes to 321 keystrokes, whose 320 paced gaps alone\n95- * are 160 s, so a fixed total would silently abort every such sequence\n96- * mid-prompt. Bounds how long the terminal lock can be held; the answer lease\n97- * is re-extended immediately before every write, so its TTL only has to cover\n98- * one gap plus one write, never the whole sequence.\n99- */\n--\n110- *\n111- * This is PACING, not a guard: it consults no screen, transcript, renderer,\n112- * session or lock state