adline/lease failure. Run focused bun tests + scoped Biome. Do not commit/push or invoke skills. Report files and tests.","result":"","isRawTranscript":true}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8497cb82-5fa0-47b6-9abd-4c45f7b5b46c","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"ca3c50ca-6a2a-4c43-8ed3-ff38d09fab96","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Verify installed desktop build","description":"Confirmed installed Superset 1.20.0 from executable and uninstall metadata, running app process tree, visible nonblank renderer, and digest-verified installer/build mapping to the final shipped build. Packaged metadata does not independently expose the commit SHA.","activeForm":"Verifying installed desktop build","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Inspect companion runtime","description":"Confirmed installed host-service and PTY daemon are running from app.asar; daemon v0.4.0 manifest advertises protocol v3. Current restart logs contain no answer attempts or guard failures yet. Detected installed Claude CLI 2.1.228 versus byte contract proven on 2.1.226, requiring live answer E2E.","activeForm":"Inspecting companion runtime","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Run closed-loop emulator E2E","description":"Completed live post-restart companion E2E on Claude CLI 2.1.228. A real physical-phone free-text request was durably confirmed in 5 ms with null failure and empty guards; a separate safe emulator single-select request also durably confirmed with protocol-v3 daemon active. The scratch status parser expected the old response shape, but ledger proof confirmed success.","activeForm":"Running closed-loop emulator E2E","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Test availability boundaries","description":"Verified renderer-visible/nonblank post-restart state and proved live phone free-text bytes reached protocol-v3 PTY and durable ledger with no guards. A genuine display-off/Windows-lock test is not currently executable: Windows automation cannot cross the lock screen and no phone/watch is connected via ADB. This limitation is reported explicitly rather than treating headless architecture as E2E proof.","activeForm":"Testing availability boundaries","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Eliminate emulator identity interference","description":"Pairing log prerequisite and isolated-emulator support code are built and published in final ARM64 run 31605016224 on SHA 4a9978200. Creating the actual separate emulator identity and repeating physical locked-screen E2E requires installing the new build, which awaits explicit exact-time authorization.","activeForm":"Eliminating emulator identity interference","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Remove secret-bearing pairing log","description":"Removed secret-bearing QR URI from production pairing logs; only non-secret pairingRef and expiry are logged. Simplify completed, full companion tests/markers/REFERR/Biome passed, two low code reviews found nothing, and commits were pushed to main.","activeForm":"Removing secret-bearing pairing log","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"Prove PTY consumption failure","description":"Incident proven end-to-end from safe metadata: the phone answer targeted the exact Claude session/picker; matching AskUser tool_result appeared 341 ms after phone intake. The answer did work, but the visible terminal failed to repaint, leaving a stale picker frame. Root cause is premature QuestionStore resolve/retract at 5 ms PTY acknowledgment plus no non-vetoing repaint nudge. Fix should preserve confirmed semantics, defer question settlement to positive PostToolUse/tool_result, and nudge repaint best-effort without becoming a barrier.","activeForm":"Proving PTY consumption failure","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"8","subject":"Fix stale picker settlement","description":"Implemented and pushed stale-picker fix: confirmed PTY writes retain pending discovery until exact positive PostToolUse/tool_result settlement, remote provenance survives races, repaint is best-effort/non-vetoing, and durable claimed→in_flight arbitration prevents fresh request retyping. Real SQLite and full companion tests pass.","activeForm":"Fixing stale picker settlement","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"9","subject":"Validate real SQLite fence","description":"Added real SQLite fence coverage and fixed issues it exposed: nullable questionId narrowing and claimed-status mapping. Tests prove confirmed/in-flight/unconfirmed fence across DB/ledger recreation, same request ID is excluded, and failed does not fence. 3/3 pass; scoped Biome clean.","activeForm":"Validating real SQLite fence","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"10","subject":"Fix review race defects","description":"Fixed both verified races: claimed/pre-write faults persist failed and remain retryable; PostToolUse-first settlement receives a corrective phone/watch provenance event. Added production-path event and zero-write retry tests. Full companion suite 219 pass, focused races 45 pass, REFERR/markers/Biome clean, simplify completed, code review found nothing. Pushed commits 692ce7dae and 4a9978200; final build 31605016224 running.","activeForm":"Fixing review race defects","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"11","subject":"Root-cause four-question partial answer","description":"Root cause confirmed from untouched live state and safe logs: phone submitted all four valid selects; bridge encoded five correct frames (four selects + final Enter) and PTY acknowledged them all in 82 ms. Claude consumed only frame 1 before its TUI transition; frames 2-5 arrived before question 2 state was ready and were ignored/misapplied. No AskUser tool_result followed. Installed 7e0d25f3c falsely retracted on PTY ack; published 4a9978200 fixes false settlement but not immediate frame sequencing, so installation alone will not fix N>1.","activeForm":"Root-causing partial multi-question answer","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"12","subject":"Prove multi-question transition race","description":"Controlled Claude Code 2.1.228 N=4 synthetic proof reproduced the race twice in burst mode: all five writes acknowledged in ~1 ms while the picker had not transitioned; subsequent frames were dropped/misapplied and no tool_result appeared. Transition-paced mode passed twice with all four answer items in tool_result. A fixed-gap sweep is continuing to select a conservative production delay.","activeForm":"Running paced control run","owner":"safe-harness","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"13","subject":"Implement non-vetoing sequence pacing","description":"Implement deterministic, non-vetoing inter-frame pacing in answer injectSequence after the real Claude 2.1.228 N=4 threshold/repeat proof establishes a conservative delay. Preserve daemon acknowledgments, durable fencing, terminal lock, lease extension, deadline checks, v2 complete-sequence fallback, and all guardless/headless behavior.","activeForm":"Implementing sequence pacing","owner":"main","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"14","subject":"Validate paced answer delivery","description":"Validated the sequencing race and fixed-gap behavior against isolated real Claude Code 2.1.228. Burst N=4 failed twice; fixed 100/250/500/1000ms current trials each produced exact four-answer tool_result; transition-observed pacing passed twice around 750–820ms. Recommended conservative 500ms deterministic inter-frame delay. No production code changed in this proof worker.","activeForm":"Validating paced answer delivery","owner":"n4-pacing-proof","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"15","subject":"Simplify and review pacing fix","description":"Invoke /simplify fully, commit the production change, then invoke /code-review low and resolve findings before shipment.","activeForm":"Simplifying and reviewing pacing fix","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"16","subject":"Publish ARM64 pacing fix","description":"Push main and run the full Windows ARM64 GitHub build/release workflow. Do not install without exact-time approval.","activeForm":"Publishing ARM64 pacing fix","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":16},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b73ea0fc-00c0-4922-8f3a-1260bb6954a5","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:38:55.877Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
