{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:57:25.812Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"general-purpose\">\nAltitude finding:\nC:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:350 — The answer orchestrator reconstructs the encoder’s maximum legal frame count from `MAX_QUESTIONS_PER_PROMPT` and `MAX_DIGIT_ADDRESSABLE_INDEX`; pacing itself is correctly centralized in `injectSequence`, but its bound/deadline policy is at the wrong abstraction. Generalize as an encoder-owned `EncodedAnswerSequence`/`AnswerSequencePlan` carrying validated frames and its execution budget (or at minimum export the bound from `keystrokes.ts`) so the injector only executes the contract. Maintenance cost: every future picker grammar/keystroke-shape change must update a non-obvious duplicate formula in `answer.ts` and its numeric test, otherwise legal sequences can be rejected or lease/deadline bounds silently diverge from the encoder.\nNo other altitude findings in the scoped diff.\n</agent-message>"}
