{"parentUuid":"ab697557-7a7a-439f-8c95-1620e29300d9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5548f27b-2b1d-4e0e-84da-bd27822c3dc9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Another Claude session sent a message:\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"t3-terminal-explorer\" color=\"purple\" summary=\"T3 findings: no PTY answer path, not comparable\">\nT3 exploration complete. Bottom line: **not comparable — nothing to port for multi-question pacing.**\n\n## Repos\n- **t3.chat is NOT open source.** No public repo. Only third-party clones (TGlide/thom-chat etc.).\n- **T3 Code IS**: https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code — MIT, 18,378 stars, pushedAt 2026-08-12T16:40:36Z.\n- Read at commit `b73232bdd31e83914a8a943960c7dc4b6390b39b`. Shallow clone (depth 200) in gitignored scratch `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\t3code-probe`. No project file modified.\n\n## Headline\nT3 Code **never answers agent questions through a PTY**. Claude runs as an SDK subprocess (`@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` `query({...})`) — `apps/server/src/provider/Layers/ClaudeAdapter.ts:22`, `:1653`. Zero `PtyAdapter`/`node-pty` refs anywhere under `apps/server/src/provider/`.\n\n`AskUserQuestion` handled in the SDK `canUseTool` callback, answered **atomically as one object** — `ClaudeAdapter.ts:3770-3895`: emit `user-input.requested` with all questions (`:3810`) → block on one `Deferred` (`:3852`) → return `{behavior:\"allow\", updatedInput:{questions, answers}}` (`:3889-3894`). Answers arrive by RPC `respondToUserInput` (`:4509-4524`). Codex: `CodexAdapter.ts:1903`. Cursor/Grok/OpenCode: ACP `session/request_permission`.\n\n→ Multi-step input, pacing, settlement detection, transition races structurally cannot occur in their answer path.\n\n## Their PTY layer (apps/server/src/terminal/)\n- write = synchronous `process.write(data)`, fire-and-forget, ack no stronger than yours — `Manager.ts:2528-2549`, `NodePtyAdapter.ts:81-83`\n- write **deliberately NOT under the per-thread semaphore** (only open/attach/resize/clear/restart/close are) — `Manager.ts:2307,2310,2568,2571,2593,2673`; lock `:1297-1301`\n- client write concurrency = default `mode:\"parallel\"` — `packages/client-runtime/src/state/terminal.ts:64-67`, default `state/runtime.ts:356`\n- settlement/quiescence: **none exists** (grep clean)\n- busy detection: 1s poll of process tree, activity label only — `Manager.ts:2067-2152`, const `:79`; Windows = `powershell.exe Get-CimInstance Win32_Process`, `:623-695`\n- resize: plain `process.resize`, no repaint/SIGWINCH nudge — `Manager.ts:203-220`, `:2551-2568`; client coalesces `mode:\"latest\"` — `client-runtime/src/state/terminal.ts:68-73`\n- output: drain queue + 40ms persist debounce, 5000-line cap — `Manager.ts:77-78`, `:1420`\n\n**Every synthetic PTY write in the repo — 2 sites, both single-shot:**\n1. `apps/server/src/project/ProjectSetupScriptRunner.ts:159-164` — `${script.command}\\r` fired immediately after open, **no readiness wait at all**\n2. `apps/mobile/src/features/terminal/ThreadTerminalRouteScreen.tsx:607-633` — launch `initialInput`, gated only on `terminal.version !== 0` + an idempotency key ref\n\nNo arrow-key/menu sequences, no inter-write delay, no echo verification anywhere.\n\n## The only genuinely useful items\n1. **Windows ConPTY TERM fix** — `NodePtyAdapter.ts:144-150`: node-pty writes `name` into child `TERM` on the Unix path only; ConPTY leaves env untouched → children get missing/16-color TERM unless injected. Shipped as `fix(server): advertise 256-color TERM on Windows terminals (#5693)`. Directly relevant to our ARM64 TUI rendering.\n2. **Per-key concurrency lanes** — `packages/client-runtime/src/state/runtime.ts:89-246`: `serial` (FIFO per key) / `singleFlight` / `latest`. Clean shape if we want per-terminal FIFO ordering. **Ordering only — does not wait on terminal state**, so it does not solve our transition race.\n3. **Answer-key contract**, issue https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/issues/2388 (closed): Claude CLI 2.1.121 changed `mapToolResultToToolResultBlockParam` to look answers up **by full question text**; T3 keyed by `header` → model got `\"User has answered your questions: .\"`. Codified at `ClaudeAdapter.ts:3782-3786`. Header is not a stable key.\n4. **Mirrors of our fence work**: https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/issues/5119 (pending AskUserQuestion leaks on teardown → thread unanswerable) and /5454 (pending popup undismissable after provider session dies) — the in-memory pending-Map failure mode our host.db ledger avoids.\n\n## Do NOT cite as precedent\n- 180ms `TERMINAL_BUFFER_REPLAY_STABILITY_DELAY_MS` (`apps/mobile/src/features/terminal/terminalBufferReplay.ts:3`) is a **render-side** replay delay, not input pacing.\n- Their input ack is weaker than our protocol-v3 `input-ok`, so there is no stronger model to borrow.\n- Ghostty (WASM/libghostty) is their renderer; xterm.js comparisons don't transfer.\n\n## Non-claims\n- History not fully examined (depth 200) — `git log -- apps/server/src/terminal` showing 3 commits is NOT evidence of absence of past pacing work.\n- No runtime testing; all statements are source reads at the stated commit.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"t3-terminal-explorer\" color=\"purple\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"t3-terminal-explorer\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:10:01.750Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"n4-pacing-proof\" color=\"yellow\" summary=\"Pacing race proven: burst drops keystrokes, paced green\">\nPROVEN, both claims, controlled + content-safe. CLI = claude-code 2.1.228 (npm global win32-arm64 claude.exe), node v22.23.1, repo main @ 7e0d25f3c.\n\nHarness: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pty-proof-4q\\proof-4q.mjs (reuses @lydell/node-pty 1.1.0 + @xterm/headless from repo node_modules; fresh temp cwd per run; synthetic labels only). Prompt: one AskUserQuestion call, 4 single-select questions (headers CanaryOne..CanaryFou, options AlphaN/BetaN). Sequence = exact encodeMany single_select_many bytes: [\"2\",\"1\",\"2\",\"1\",\"\\r\"] → expected Beta1,Alpha2,Beta3,Alpha4. Commands: `node proof-4q.mjs burst r1|r2`, `node proof-4q.mjs paced r2|r3`. Artifacts: {mode}-{run}-RESULT.json + numbered screen snapshots in same dir. (paced-r1 = discarded harness-defect run: needles matched prompt echo, digits typed pre-picker — ignore.)\n\nCLAIM 1 — ack precedes TUI transition: YES, definitively. Burst runs: all 5 writes returned (ack analog; never later than daemon pty.write ack) within ~1ms total (burst-r1: 49580.91→49581.35ms), while screen at EVERY ack still showed Q1 untouched (tab bar all ☐, caret on Alpha1). First visible transition ~100-400ms after last ack. Same pre-transition stateAtAck on every paced frame.\n\nCLAIM 2 — burst reproduces partial advance: YES, 2/2 identical. Burst: TUI later applies ONLY the first 2 digits (☒ CanaryOne, ☒ CanaryTwo), then digits 3+4 and the review \\r are swallowed; picker stuck open on Q3 (caret Alpha3) from ~500ms through 9.5s and final; tool_result NEVER appears. Note: stall depth here = 2 questions vs the real incident's 1 — timing-dependent prefix length, same structural class (prefix applied, tail dropped, prompt never submitted, no tool_result).\n\nCONTROL — paced: 2/2 fully green. Waiting for the observed per-question transition before each next keystroke (measured gaps ~750-820ms) → all 4 tabs ☒, caret lands on Submit, \\r submits, picker closes, tool_result carries all 4 expected labels correctly attributed (\"one?\"=\"Beta1\", \"two?\"=\"Alpha2\", \"three?\"=\"Beta3\", \"four?\"=\"Alpha4\").\n\nBonus (contract-relevant): 2.1.228 N>1 picker renders a NEW tab-bar UI vs 2.1.226 notes in keystrokes.ts — `←  ☐ CanaryOne … ✔ Submit  →`, footer \"Enter to select · Tab/Arrow keys to navigate · Esc to cancel\"; per-question numbered rows incl. \"3. Type something.\" + \"4. Chat about this\". Byte semantics UNCHANGED when paced (digit selects+advances, final screen = Submit tab, \\r submits). PROVEN_AGAINST still says 2.1.226; render drifted, bytes hold — but only under pacing.\n\nImplication for task #13: daemon input acknowledgment is NOT consumption on 2.1.228; zero-delay acknowledged writes deterministically lose keystrokes across question-advance renders. Pacing on observed TUI transition (what ScreenExpectation/guard-5 already models) fixes it 2/2. No production files touched.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-architect\" color=\"orange\" summary=\"Blueprint: adaptive per-keystroke pacing, non-vetoing\">\nBLUEPRINT — headless answer pacing (ANSWER-PACING)\n\nROOT MECHANISM CONFIRMED IN CODE\nDaemon ack = `session.pty.write()` returned (packages/pty-daemon/src/handlers/handlers.ts:120-133; packages/host-service/src/terminal/DaemonClient/DaemonClient.ts:204-210). That proves bytes queued into ConPTY pipe — NOT that Claude's Ink loop consumed them. 5 acks in 82ms → digits 2-4 + \\r land during picker's Q1→Q2 unmount/remount window → dropped. Frames are already discrete per keystroke on protocol-v3 (answer.ts:1440-1445); the only missing piece is a gap between them keyed to actual consumption.\n\n1. RECOMMENDED APPROACH — option (4): host-side adaptive pacing on the emulator mirror, with a fixed floor and a cap fallback; strictly time-shaping, never outcome-shaping.\nAfter each acknowledged non-final keystroke: wait ≥ FLOOR, then poll host's headless-xterm screen until it differs from the pre-write snapshot, cap at TIMEOUT, then write the next keystroke regardless. Mirror is renderer-independent and headless: every PTY output byte feeds `session.modeTracker` in `deliverOutput` (packages/host-service/src/terminal/terminal.ts:1366-1372) even with zero sockets; `snapshotSession` reads it (terminal.ts:1252-1273); companion already wires it as `deps.snapshotScreen` (packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts:2012-2063). Screen-change-after-write = the TUI repainted = it consumed the byte; that is the earliest safe send point and it adapts to load (emulated ARM64, heavy repaints).\n\nAlternatives and why they lose:\n- (1) fixed delay only: constant tuned on one machine re-creates the race class under load, or inflates every answer if sized for worst case. Kept only as the embedded fallback (floor+cap ARE fixed delays when the mirror is unreadable/static).\n- (2) per-question grouping + delay: intra-question bytes still race (multiselect toggle repaints), a multi-byte chunk against Ink is itself an unproven shape (keystrokes.ts's whole policy), and it breaks the per-keystroke ack accounting (`written`, `abortedAt`) that unconfirmed-reporting depends on (answer.ts:1440-1516).\n- (3) daemon-side ack barrier: `pty.write` return / event-loop turn / next-output are all still upstream of Ink's input handling — wrong layer; daemon can't know keystroke semantics; requires protocol-v4 (messages.ts) + skew handling with detached older daemons; slows every acked write. Host already sees the same output stream, so nothing is gained.\n\n2. FILES\n- C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts — all production changes:\n  a) constants: `KEYSTROKE_PACE_FLOOR_MS = 40`, `KEYSTROKE_PACE_TIMEOUT_MS = 250` (reuse existing `SCREEN_ADVANCE_POLL_MS = 25`, answer.ts:84).\n  b) new helper `paceUntilScreenAdvance(deps, terminalId, preScreen)` — NOT `awaitScreenAdvance` (answer.ts:1546): that returns null immediately on unreadable mirror, which for pacing would mean ZERO delay = today's race. New helper: sleep floor; then poll via `safeSnapshot` (answer.ts:1525, never throws); return early on `snap !== pre` (only when pre non-null); otherwise run out the cap. Returns a stats tag (advanced|timeout|unobservable) for logging only. Cannot throw, cannot veto.\n  c) `injectSequence` (answer.ts:1406-1519): take `pre = await safeSnapshot(...)` before each write that has a successor frame; after `written += ...` (answer.ts:1515), if not last frame, `await paceUntilScreenAdvance(...)`. Use `question.terminalId` (wire handle — PendingQuestion carries it, question-store.ts:570; same id `safeSnapshot` takes everywhere else).\n  d) deadline scaling: `deadlineMs = now + SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS + (keystrokes.length - 1) * KEYSTROKE_PACE_TIMEOUT_MS` (replaces answer.ts:1425). Base 10s stays the write/ack budget; pacing budget added exactly per gap, so pacing alone can NEVER trip the deadline abort at answer.ts:1464 — that abort would be a pacing-caused downgrade, forbidden. Export a pure `sequenceDeadlineMs(count)` for tests. Lease safe: `extend` per frame resets 15s TTL (answer.ts:1468; config.ts:141 answerLeaseTtlMs), gaps ≤250ms.\n  e) one summary log line per sequence (`companion.answer.paced`: counts + total pace ms).\n  f) module-header + (ANSWER-GUARDLESS) comment updates (answer.ts:1-20, 1390-1404): screen is now read for PACING; still may never veto/downgrade.\n- C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts — the test at :466-495 currently pins `snapshotScreen: forbidden` (throws if consulted). Reframe invariant from \"never read\" to \"read can never change outcome\": throwing snapshotScreen still confirms with all bytes written (exercises unobservable fallback). Add: (i) advancing-screen stub → confirmed, snapshot/write interleave order correct; (ii) static screen → confirmed after cap fallback; (iii) no pace after final keystroke; (iv) `sequenceDeadlineMs` unit test (don't real-time a 41-keystroke static-screen run).\n- C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\FEATURES.md — add `(ANSWER-PACING)` to the Companion bridge row's marker list + markers block entry `(ANSWER-PACING)\tpackages/host-service/src/companion`, SAME commit as code (BF lesson).\n\n3. DATA FLOW (single-select ×4 = 5 keystrokes)\n/v1/answer → validate/encode (unchanged, pre-lock) → lease + terminal lock → per frame k: deadline check → lease extend → snapshot pre_k (mirror, in-process) → `writer.write` → daemon `pty.write` → input-ok → written++ → if k<last: sleep 40ms, poll mirror ≤250ms for change vs pre_k → next frame. Confirmation still = all acks (unchanged); ledger readback unchanged; repaint nudge unchanged. Typical added latency ≈ 4 × (40ms + one repaint ~50-100ms) ≈ 0.4-0.6s; worst (static/unreadable mirror) 4×250ms = 1s.\n\n4. BUILD ORDER\n1. `sequenceDeadlineMs` + constants + unit test. 2. `paceUntilScreenAdvance` + tests (throwing/static/advancing stubs). 3. Wire into `injectSequence`; update the forbidden-source test. 4. Comments + FEATURES.md marker. 5. Live E2E: real 4-question picker via phone path, assert `tool_result` carries all four answers (only ground truth the contract accepts).\n\n5. RISKS / EDGE CASES\n- Spurious screen change (spinner/animation) → early release: floor guarantees ≥40ms gap (observed failure was <20ms back-to-back); cap-bounded worst case still ≥25ms poll spacing. If E2E shows 40ms floor insufficient during question-transition remount, raise FLOOR — one constant.\n- Unreadable mirror (adoption race, `snapshotScreen` throws via liveness lookup in companion/index.ts:2012): safeSnapshot → null → full-cap fixed delay. Never a veto — constraint honored even though the snapshot path internally touches liveness.\n- Long sequences: worst proven shape (4 multiselect × 9 toggles + 4 arrows + \\r = 41 keystrokes) → pacing ≤10s + base 10s; lock held up to ~20s; concurrent /v1/message waiter times out at LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS 5s with honest \"terminal was busy; nothing was written\" (answer.ts:1883) — acceptable.\n- v2 daemon single-blob path (answer.ts:1446-1454): unpaceable, unchanged — already returns durable `unconfirmed` + stale-mark.\n- Freetext body frame: editor-open repaint and body echo both change the screen; uniform per-frame pacing covers freetext/multiselect groups with no shape-specific logic.\n- Settlement (PostToolUse-driven) untouched; pacing cannot delay or suppress it.\n\n6. OUT OF SCOPE\nDaemon/protocol changes; /v1/message path (has its own echo waits); v2-daemon pacing; picker byte contract (PROVEN_AGAINST untouched); any new guard, veto, or outcome state; renderer/UX changes.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-architect\" color=\"orange\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pacing-architect\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:19:38.254Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pty-barrier-analysis\" color=\"pink\" summary=\"PTY output cannot prove picker consumption\">\nDeep result: there is no meaningful PTY consumption barrier available in the current stack. Protocol-v3 `input-ok` is emitted immediately after synchronous `session.pty.write(...)` returns (`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\handlers\\handlers.ts:120-133`); the adapter merely calls node-pty/ConPTY `term.write` (`...\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\Pty\\Pty.ts:315-318`). Output arrives independently later through `term.onData` (`Pty.ts:330-333`) and daemon broadcast (`...\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\Server\\Server.ts:559-578`). Protocol output frames have only `{type,id}`, no seq/request correlation (`...\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\protocol\\messages.ts:122-133`). Host `outputSeq` is a renderer catch-up byte counter, not a consumption counter (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\terminal.ts:460-477,1320-1334,1360-1372`), and DaemonClient routes output only to session callbacks while input-ok goes through request listeners (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\DaemonClient\\DaemonClient.ts:338-409,546-589`).\n\nRecommendation: use deterministic, non-vetoing pacing between logical keystroke transitions; do NOT let “first output after input” release the next key early. Raw output is temporally stronger than input-ok only in the weak sense that the child emitted *something* later; it cannot establish that the just-written key was consumed or that the picker is ready. False accelerators: spinner/background output; delayed/cached replay output during headless adoption; free-text echo beginning before the whole body is consumed; a toggle repaint emitted while React/TUI state work remains queued; terminal query/repaint traffic. False negatives: quiet transitions, identical/differential repaint suppression, buffered/coalesced screen updates. Adding daemon output sequence/request IDs would order events but not create causality. Only an application-level Claude picker ack could do that, and the repo has none.\n\nMinimal design: retain v3 ack for honest write acceptance; after each successful non-final logical frame, sleep a conservative empirically proven interval before the next frame. Every digit/toggle/right-arrow/free-text-open/body/editor-return is a transition; do not delay after the final submit. Renew the answer lease around/before waits and writes. Rework `SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS=10_000` (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:83-90`) because valid capture/answer arity is up to 32 (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\limits.ts:148-151`) and free-text can produce ~3 frames/question; a fixed 10s deadline will turn pacing into partial delivery. Existing repo precedent is 500ms separation for command text/Enter and follow-up submit (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\terminal.ts:333-350`). Pick the actual picker interval from repeated live trials, not that precedent alone.\n\nIf desired, record outputSeq deltas/timestamps as diagnostics only. They may inform a later measured interval, but must never veto, downgrade, or shorten below the proven fixed floor.\n\nTest plan: (1) unit fake PTY proves input-ok precedes delayed onData; (2) fake delayed output/no output/unsolicited output/replay output proves output-driven early release is unsound; (3) live Claude 2.1.226 repeated N=2/4/8 all-digit trials and mixed free-text first/middle/last, multi-select with multiple toggles, last-free-text consecutive returns; assert agent `tool_result`, not screen; (4) sweep candidate delays, then choose conservative margin and run 50+ repetitions under CPU load; (5) no renderer, display-off/locked, host restart+headless adoption; (6) maximum 32-question/frame-heavy sequence verifies dynamic deadline + lease renewal and no partial write; (7) injected write refusal at each frame preserves existing honest failed/unconfirmed fencing. I will send the full ordered blueprint in my final.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"t3-terminal-explorer\" color=\"purple\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"t3-terminal-explorer\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:21:38.584Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\",\"summary\":\"[to pacing-proof] T3 findings: no synthetic multi-step PTY input\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pty-barrier-analysis\" color=\"pink\" summary=\"Full PTY barrier design blueprint\">\nFull blueprint follows.\n\n1. Recommended approach\nUse deterministic pacing after every successful, non-final protocol-v3 logical input frame. Keep `input-ok` solely as proof that the daemon accepted the write. Do not implement a runtime output-after-input gate. Choose the interval only after live Claude 2.1.226 sweeps; apply one conservative floor to control transitions, and explicitly test whether a maximum-size UTF-8 free-text body needs a larger kind/length-based delay before its return. Sleep after select/toggle/free-text-open/free-text-body/nonfinal editor-return/right-arrow; never after the final submit. The sleep is unconditional, resolves normally, and cannot veto/downgrade. Lease is re-extended before each next write as today.\nAlternatives rejected: (a) first PTY output after input: no request/seq correlation or causality, and can be stale replay/background output; (b) output quiescence: quiet valid transitions false-negative and spinner/background output can defer forever; (c) daemon protocol-v4 ‘consumed’ ack: node-pty/ConPTY exposes queue/write acceptance only, so without Claude cooperation it would just rename input-ok; (d) renderer/screen/transcript: forbidden dependency and stale/missing headlessly; (e) whole v3 sequence in one write: reproduces the measured N=4 loss. Output timing can be logged for offline tuning only; it must not shorten below the proven floor, gate the next frame, or affect outcome.\nImportant deadline correction: current `SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS` is not actually a hard bound because it is checked only between awaited writes (`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1425-1466`); a hung write can already hold forever. Production DaemonClient independently times each input ack at 5s (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\DaemonClient\\DaemonClient.ts:63-66,383-391`), and the request has bounded arity 32 (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\limits.ts:148-151`). Do not allow a fixed 10s wall-clock deadline to turn intentional pacing into a partial answer. Prefer deleting the misleading overall deadline and relying on finite encoded frames + the real per-write timeout. If retained, compute it from frame count, pacing budget, and per-frame ack budget, using a monotonic clock; a forward wall-clock correction must not abort a valid paced sequence.\n\n2. Files\n- MODIFY `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts`: pacing constant/policy, non-final wait in `injectSequence`, and removal/rework of fixed 10s deadline/comment. Keep observation-free outcomes.\n- MODIFY `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts`: order/timing policy tests, no-wait-after-final, lease/write failures unchanged, clock/deadline regression, and assert no legacy guard source is consulted.\n- MODIFY `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\FEATURES.md`: update the existing companion row/marker to state acknowledged writes are paced for consumer settlement and pacing observations never veto/downgrade.\n- CREATE nothing. Specifically do not change `packages/pty-daemon`, protocol messages, DaemonClient output routing, terminal screen tracker, or client apps for this fix.\n\n3. Data flow\nAPI/Zod validates answer count/order/kinds (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\http.ts:633-698`); `encodeAnswer` emits discrete semantic frames (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\keystrokes.ts:958-986`); `handleAnswer` establishes durable write fence and terminal lock (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1084-1137`); for each v3 frame, extend lease, write raw bytes, await correlated input-ok, count the frame, then if non-final wait deterministic settlement interval; repeat. Actual write path is host adapter -> DaemonClient -> daemon `session.pty.write` (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\terminal.ts:1021-1062`; `...\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\handlers\\handlers.ts:98-133`). After final acknowledged submit, persist/read back DB ledger outcome, publish resolution and optionally nudge repaint; repaint remains diagnostic (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts:1139-1202`). v2 remains its existing one-frame whole-sequence/unconfirmed compatibility path (`answer.ts:1440-1454`); it cannot honestly pace per frame without changing its duplicate/outcome contract.\n\n4. Build order\n(1) Live sweep candidate intervals on N=4 all-digit until repeated tool_result truth, including CPU load; pick conservative margin. (2) Prove max-length UTF-8 free text at that interval; introduce a deterministic body-specific delay only if needed. (3) Add pure pacing-policy tests. (4) Wire wait after successful non-final v3 writes. (5) remove/rework fixed deadline so pacing cannot trigger partial abort. (6) Run companion unit suite and daemon acknowledged-input tests. (7) Live matrix and locked/headless lifecycle. (8) update FEATURES row with exact behavior.\n\n5. Risks/edges\n- First output is unsound: replay is delivered immediately on subscribe (`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\handlers\\handlers.ts:184-207`); headless adoption subscribes with replay by default (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\terminal.ts:2371-2378,2855-2860`); output frames carry no request/seq (`...\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\protocol\\messages.ts:122-133`). Host `outputSeq` begins at process-local adoption and counts all delivered output bytes, including replay; it is renderer catch-up, not input consumption (`terminal.ts:460-477,1320-1372`).\n- False-positive live output: spinner, focus/query traffic, repaint, background process, previous write's delayed chunk, toggle repaint before next picker is ready. Free-text echo can start before the entire body is processed. Socket/chunk coalescing destroys one-input/one-output assumptions.\n- False-negative output: state changes can be quiet, identical repaint, delayed/coalesced, or suppressed. Waiting for output would hang/downgrade valid writes.\n- Long valid sequences: 32 questions and multi-select toggles can exceed 10s once paced; test upper bound and request/client timeout behavior. The answer lease TTL is 15s (`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\config.ts:141`) but is extended before every frame (`answer.ts:1468-1478`), so interval must stay well below TTL.\n- Pacing cannot repair a write already directed at a stale picker; durable identity/fence remain responsible. Observations cannot become a new stale/session/screen veto.\n- v2 cannot get honest per-frame pacing with current acknowledged writer contract; document as compatibility limitation, do not silently report confirmation.\n\n6. Test plan\nUnit: record write/wait order for every keystroke kind; exactly N-1 waits; final submit has no trailing wait; wait occurs only after success; refusal/throw stops with existing written/abortedAt/writeOutcome; lease extension runs before every write after wait; a wait never changes result; fixed-deadline regression with >10s modeled pacing; no screen/transcript/session/binding/permission calls. Daemon adversarial: fake PTY where write returns now/onData later proves input-ok-before-output; no-output, unsolicited-output, delayed prior-output, replay-output, and coalesced-output cases prove no safe output gate. Live truth matrix (agent tool_result is oracle): N=2/4/8/32 all digit; free text first/middle/last/both and max UTF-8 body; multi-select first/middle/last with 1 and 9 toggles; last free text’s consecutive returns; repeated >=50 under CPU load. Lifecycle: zero renderer, display off, Windows lock, renderer reconnect, host restart/headless adoption. Failure injection at every frame preserves durable failed/unconfirmed fence. Compare identical journeys before/after and capture frame/ack/wait timestamps; output timestamps are diagnostic only.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pty-barrier-analysis\" color=\"pink\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pty-barrier-analysis\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:30:17.739Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-architect\" color=\"orange\" summary=\"Constants revised: floor 100ms, cap 500ms\">\nBlueprint amendment (constants only), after multistep-byte-analysis's empirical runs (fixed 100/250/500/1000ms each passed once; burst failed 2/2):\n\n- KEYSTROKE_PACE_FLOOR_MS: 40 → 100 (lowest empirically-passing fixed delay; adaptive never releases earlier, so a spurious screen change still yields a proven-safe gap).\n- KEYSTROKE_PACE_TIMEOUT_MS: 250 → 500 (cap; unreadable/static mirror degrades to exactly fixed-500ms, the minimal-reliable fixed candidate).\n- Deadline scaling accordingly: `SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS + (n-1) * 500`. Worst proven shape (41 keystrokes, static mirror) ≈ 20s pacing + 10s base lock-hold — /v1/message waiters still fail honest at 5s lock wait.\n\nEverything else in the blueprint unchanged. Adaptive stays the recommendation over pure fixed 500ms: fixed is open-loop (n=1 samples, load-sensitive), adaptive waits on evidence of consumption (repaint after acked write) and contains fixed-500 as its worst case.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pty-barrier-analysis\" color=\"pink\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pty-barrier-analysis\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:33:07.103Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\",\"summary\":\"[to multistep-byte-analysis] Use fixed pacing, never PTY output barrier\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-architect\" color=\"orange\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pacing-architect\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:33:17.890Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\",\"summary\":\"[to multistep-byte-analysis] Adaptive pacing > fixed 500ms; floor 100, cap 500\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"t3-terminal-explorer\" color=\"purple\" summary=\"Precise t3code citations, files/lines, reusables\">\nIndependent citations. All read directly at pinned commit `b73232bdd31e83914a8a943960c7dc4b6390b39b` (pingdotgg/t3code, MIT). Permalinks below are that sha, so they are stable.\n\n## Repo identity\n- t3.chat: **no public repo** (not open source). Third-party clones only.\n- T3 Code: https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code — 18,378 stars, pushedAt 2026-08-12T16:40:36Z, default branch `main`.\n- Local read-only clone: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\t3code-probe` (gitignored, depth 200). Nothing in the project modified.\n\n## A. Answer path is SDK, never PTY\n- https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/blob/b73232bdd31e83914a8a943960c7dc4b6390b39b/apps/server/src/provider/Layers/ClaudeAdapter.ts#L22 — imports `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`; `query({` at `#L1653`.\n- `.../ClaudeAdapter.ts#L3770-L3895` — `handleAskUserQuestion`: emits `user-input.requested` with ALL questions (`#L3810`), blocks on ONE `Deferred` (`#L3852`), returns `{behavior:\"allow\", updatedInput:{questions, answers}}` (`#L3889-L3894`).\n- `.../ClaudeAdapter.ts#L4509-L4524` — `respondToUserInput` → `Deferred.succeed`.\n- `.../CodexAdapter.ts#L1903`; Cursor/Grok/OpenCode use ACP `session/request_permission` (`.../CursorAdapter.ts#L1086`, `.../GrokAdapter.ts#L1369`).\n- Negative evidence: no `PtyAdapter`/`node-pty`/`pty` match anywhere under `apps/server/src/provider/`.\n\n## B. PTY layer facts (apps/server/src/terminal/)\n- `.../terminal/Manager.ts#L2528-L2549` — `write` = `Effect.try(() => process.write(input.data))`. Fire-and-forget; ack no stronger than \"did not throw\".\n- `.../terminal/NodePtyAdapter.ts#L81-L83` — adapter `write` is a bare passthrough.\n- `.../terminal/Manager.ts#L1297-L1301` — `withThreadLock` (per-thread semaphore). Applied at `#L2307`, `#L2310`, `#L2568`, `#L2571`, `#L2593`, `#L2673` = open/attach/resize/clear/restart/close. **`write` is absent from that list — deliberately unserialized.**\n- `.../packages/client-runtime/src/state/terminal.ts#L64-L67` — client `write` command declares no scheduler/concurrency → default `mode:\"parallel\"` (`.../state/runtime.ts#L356`).\n- **No settlement/quiescence anywhere.** Grep for settle/quiescen/awaitIdle/idleFor across `apps/server/src` returns only unrelated thread-lifecycle domain events (`orchestration/decider.pinned.test.ts` etc.).\n- `.../terminal/Manager.ts#L2067-L2152` — 1s process-tree poll → `activity` event + child-command label. Interval const `#L79` (`DEFAULT_SUBPROCESS_POLL_INTERVAL_MS = 1_000`).\n- `.../terminal/Manager.ts#L623-L695` — Windows inspector: single `powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command \"Get-CimInstance Win32_Process ...\"`, 1500ms timeout, descendant-PID walk. POSIX variant `#L697-L745` (pgrep + ps).\n- `.../terminal/Manager.ts#L203-L220` and `#L2551-L2568` — resize = plain `process.resize`. No repaint nudge, no SIGWINCH trick, no post-resize wait.\n- `.../packages/client-runtime/src/state/terminal.ts#L68-L73` — resize coalesced `mode:\"latest\"`; lane impl `.../state/runtime.ts#L207-L246`.\n- `.../terminal/Manager.ts#L77-L78` — `DEFAULT_HISTORY_LINE_LIMIT = 5_000`, `DEFAULT_PERSIST_DEBOUNCE_MS = 40`; debounce used at `#L1420`.\n- `.../apps/web/src/terminal/ghostty/core.ts#L504-L525` — bracketed paste is client-side only; server byte-transparent.\n\n## C. Every synthetic PTY write in the repo (exhaustive — two sites)\n1. https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/blob/b73232bdd31e83914a8a943960c7dc4b6390b39b/apps/server/src/project/ProjectSetupScriptRunner.ts#L159-L164 — `data: \\`${script.command}\\r\\`` fired immediately after `terminalManager.open` (`#L141-L158`). No prompt-readiness wait, no settlement check.\n2. https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/blob/b73232bdd31e83914a8a943960c7dc4b6390b39b/apps/mobile/src/features/terminal/ThreadTerminalRouteScreen.tsx#L607-L633 — launch `initialInput`, gated only on `terminal.version !== 0` plus `sentInitialInputKeyRef` idempotency.\n\nNo arrow-key/menu sequences, no inter-write delay, no echo verification anywhere in the tree.\n\n## D. Reusable mechanisms (honest ranking)\n1. **Per-key concurrency lanes** — `packages/client-runtime/src/state/runtime.ts#L89-L246`: `serial` (FIFO per key) / `singleFlight` / `latest` (coalesce to newest). The only structurally reusable piece. **Ordering only; never waits on terminal state** → does not by itself solve our transition race.\n2. **Windows ConPTY TERM injection** — `apps/server/src/terminal/NodePtyAdapter.ts#L144-L150`: node-pty writes `name` into the child's `TERM` on the Unix path only; ConPTY leaves env untouched, so Windows children inherit missing/16-color `TERM` unless set explicitly. Shipped as commit `c14bcca1 fix(server): advertise 256-color TERM on Windows terminals (#5693)`. Rendering fidelity, not pacing.\n3. **Answer-key contract** — https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/issues/2388 (closed): Claude CLI 2.1.121 changed `mapToolResultToToolResultBlockParam` to key answers **by full question text**; T3 keyed by `header` → model received `\"User has answered your questions: .\"` (answer silently dropped, while T3's own `user-input.resolved` log looked correct). Codified `ClaudeAdapter.ts#L3782-L3786`. Header is not a stable key.\n4. **Failure modes mirroring our fence/ledger work** — https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/issues/5119 (pending AskUserQuestion leaks on session teardown → thread unanswerable and unsettleable) and https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/issues/5454 (pending user-input popup undismissable after provider session dies). Both are the in-memory pending-`Map` class our host.db ledger avoids. Also open: https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/issues/6344 (multiSelect commits on first click, reopened after #6027 closed unfixed).\n\n## E. Explicit non-reusables / traps\n- Their input ack is **weaker** than our protocol-v3 `input-ok` — no stronger acknowledgment model to adopt.\n- `TERMINAL_BUFFER_REPLAY_STABILITY_DELAY_MS = 180` (`apps/mobile/src/features/terminal/terminalBufferReplay.ts#L3`) is a **render-side** replay stability delay. It is NOT input pacing and must not be cited to justify an inter-answer delay constant.\n- Ghostty (web WASM + iOS/Android libghostty) is their renderer; xterm.js comparisons do not transfer.\n\n## F. Non-claims\n- Clone is `--depth 200`, so `git log -- apps/server/src/terminal` showing only 3 commits (`c14bcca1`, `c30a6d9b`, `37ae1abb`) is NOT evidence that pacing work never existed upstream of that window.\n- No runtime execution or testing of T3 Code. Every statement is a source read at the stated commit.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"t3-terminal-explorer\" color=\"purple\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"t3-terminal-explorer\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:33:34.158Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pty-barrier-analysis\" color=\"pink\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pty-barrier-analysis\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:34:39.276Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\",\"summary\":\"[to multistep-byte-analysis] One dynamic deadline caution\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-architect\" color=\"orange\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pacing-architect\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:34:46.317Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\",\"summary\":\"[to multistep-byte-analysis] Concur; fixed pacing carry-over requirements listed\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-implementation\" color=\"cyan\" summary=\"Pacing fix implemented; 226 tests pass, Biome clean\">\nPacing fix implemented in worktree. Not committed/pushed; no /simplify; no unrelated files touched.\n\nChanges:\n1. packages/host-service/src/companion/answer.ts\n   - New exported `INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS = 500` (doc records 2.1.228 proof: burst 2/2 fail, 100/250/500/1000ms pass; conservative pick; pacing-not-guard contract stated).\n   - `AnswerDeps.wait(ms)` — injected pacing sleep (duration-only, structurally cannot veto). `assertAnswerDeps` now fails loud when unwired.\n   - `injectSequence`:\n     * Dynamic deadline: `SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS + (frames-1) × INTER_KEYSTROKE_DELAY_MS`, v3-acknowledged path only; legacy v2 keeps bare 10s. `SEQUENCE_DEADLINE_MS` comment derives max legal sequence: 32 questions × (9 toggles + arrow) + review return = 321 keystrokes → 160s pacing budget, why fixed total was unusable.\n     * Sleep AFTER every non-final acknowledged discrete keystroke (covers editor-open/body/return, toggles, arrows, question transitions, final review transition); none after final frame; none on the v2 single legacy frame (v2 stays one complete frame, honest `unconfirmed`).\n     * Lease extension unchanged at loop top → occurs after the prior sleep, immediately before each actual write (requirement 3 satisfied by ordering, verified by test). Lease TTL only needs one gap+write; unchanged.\n     * A throwing `wait` is logged (`companion.answer.pacing_wait_failed` — ids only, no answer/body content) and skipped — pacing can never veto/downgrade landed bytes.\n   - Header + injectSequence doc comments updated.\n2. packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts — composition root wires `wait: (ms) => sleep(ms)`.\n3. FEATURES.md — `(ANSWER-GUARDLESS)` row wording extended (500ms v3 pacing, state-blind/non-vetoing, lease re-extended post-delay pre-write, deadline widens by pacing budget for 32-question max, v2 frame never paced). Marker tokens untouched; `node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` → all 147 present.\n4. answer-guardless.test.ts — stubs gained `wait`; new `(ANSWER-PACING)` describe, 7 tests: exact delay placement on freetext open/body/return timeline (extend→write→wait ordering, no trailing wait), wait→extend→write ordering, zero waits on legacy v2 (single joined frame), 25-frame sequence with 12s of clock-advancing sleeps confirms (fails under old fixed deadline), genuine deadline exhaustion still aborts `unconfirmed written:1 not_written`, throwing sleep logged without downgrade, assertAnswerDeps throws on missing wait.\n\nVerification: `bun test src/companion` → 226 pass / 0 fail (full companion suite incl. new tests); scoped `bunx biome check` on 3 changed TS files → clean; marker gate green. No errors outstanding.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-implementation\" color=\"cyan\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pacing-implementation\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:41:14.793Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\",\"summary\":\"[to multistep-byte-analysis] Edits pre-dated STOP; full change/test report; standing by\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pacing-implementation\" color=\"cyan\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pacing-implementation\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:42:10.023Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"n4-pacing-proof\" color=\"yellow\" summary=\"Sweep done: 250ms silently wrong, 1000ms 3/3 safe\">\nTask #12 addendum — pacing-constant sweep done (19 PTY runs, claude 2.1.228, artifacts tmp/pty-proof-4q/). Outcomes by fixed inter-keystroke gap: burst 0/2, 25ms 0/1, 50ms 0/1, 100ms 1/3, 250ms 2/3, 500ms 3/3, 1000ms 3/3, transition-paced 2/2. CRITICAL: the 250ms failure was NOT a stall — tool_result came back with all four answers WRONG (misaligned one question, silently committed). So the race's worst mode is silent wrong answers, not lost answers; small pacing constants are actively dangerous. Recommendation delivered to multistep-byte-analysis for #13: non-vetoing primitive = pure sleep(1000ms) after each screen-advancing keystroke (select_digit N>1, submit_tab, freetext_open, editor-closing return), no gap within same-screen groups (toggle runs, freetext body→\\r), acknowledged writes + whole-sequence unconfirmed ledger fencing unchanged. Cost ~1s per question. Note: working tree has uncommitted changes to packages/host-service/src/companion/{answer.ts,index.ts,answer-guardless.test.ts} + FEATURES.md — not mine (tmp/ only); assume #13 implementer.\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"n4-pacing-proof\" color=\"yellow\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"n4-pacing-proof\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T17:52:02.154Z\",\"idleReason\":\"failed\",\"failureReason\":\"You're out of usage credits · resets 10:30pm (Europe/London)\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"t3-terminal-explorer\" color=\"purple\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"t3-terminal-explorer\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-12T18:13:11.569Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\nThis came from another Claude session — not typed by your user, but very likely working 