{"parentUuid":"0810b4c1-86c2-401b-a0aa-a65c046ac09a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\CLAUDE.md","content":{"path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"@AGENTS.md\r\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false},"displayPath":"apps\\desktop\\CLAUDE.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"130fee38-ed02-4b00-bab1-2e36c5b1c202","timestamp":"2026-08-12T18:55:33.003Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"130fee38-ed02-4b00-bab1-2e36c5b1c202","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\AGENTS.md","content":{"path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# Implementation details\r\nFor Electron interprocess communication, ALWAYS use trpc as defined in `src/lib/trpc`\r\nPlease use alias as defined in `tsconfig.json` when possible\r\n\r\n## Server-driven announcements (desktop notices)\r\n\r\nTo show an announcement/warning popup in the app without shipping a release, insert a row in the `desktop_notices` table (served by `GET /api/desktop/version`). Authoring guide — markdown-only body, severities, triggers, targeting, QA previews: `docs/DESKTOP_NOTICES.md`.\r\n\r\n## Persisted renderer state (localStorage) policy\r\n\r\nRenderer localStorage has one ~10 MB quota, loads synchronously at boot, and keys outlive the code that wrote them — unbounded growth has frozen the renderer before (23.7 MB profile, GH #5496). Every writer must be allowlisted in `src/renderer/lib/persisted-keys/persisted-key-registry.test-data.ts` (CI fails on unregistered writers), and code review must answer three questions:\r\n\r\n1. **What bounds it?** A cap/LRU, a TTL, reconciliation against an owning entity, or \"fixed-size singleton\". \"It's small per write\" is not a bound.\r\n2. **Who deletes it?** New entity-keyed data belongs in SQLite; existing stores must document their deletion path or sunset plan because deletes from CLIs or other machines can bypass UI cleanup. One-shot payloads must be cleared by their consumer. Deleting a map entry means removing the key, never writing `null`.\r\n3. **What happens when the feature dies?** Move the keys to `DEAD_KEYS` in the same PR that removes the writer; the boot sweep cleans existing profiles. Deleting the writer without registering the key strands it on user profiles forever.\r\n\r\nGuardrail: localStorage is for small singleton UI state. Anything entity-scoped with unbounded cardinality, or payloads beyond a few KB, belongs in the SQLite persistence layer (`createElectronSQLitePersistence`) — localStorage collections re-serialize the whole org blob on every mutation.\r\n\r\n## Window-drag regions: `drag` on empty leaves only\r\n\r\nNever mark a container with interactive children as `drag` and carve the children out with `no-drag`: Chromium loses the carve-outs when they sit inside masked, scrollable, or CSS-zoomed wrappers (OverflowFadeContainer, ZoomStable), which silently deadens every control under the bar. Instead, put `drag` only on dedicated empty leaf elements — traffic-light spacers and flex fillers (see TopBar, DashboardSidebarHeader, packages/panes TabBar). The worst failure mode then is \"empty area not draggable\" instead of \"chrome swallows clicks\".\r\n\r\n## Error text must be selectable\r\n\r\nThe renderer sets `user-select: none` on `body`, so rendered errors need explicit `select-text cursor-text` classes — otherwise users can't copy them into bug reports. (Sonner toasts are exempt; they manage selection themselves.)\r\n\r\n## tRPC Subscriptions (trpc-electron)\r\n\r\n**Important:** While standard tRPC recommends async generators for subscriptions, `trpc-electron` (used for Electron IPC) **only supports observables**. The library explicitly checks `isObservable(result)` and throws an error otherwise. Use the `observable` pattern:\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\n// CORRECT for trpc-electron - use observable pattern\r\nimport { observable } from \"@trpc/server/observable\";\r\n\r\nexport const createMyRouter = () => {\r\n  return router({\r\n    subscribe: publicProcedure.subscription(() => {\r\n      return observable<MyEvent>((emit) => {\r\n        const handler = (data: MyData) => {\r\n          emit.next({ type: \"my-event\", data });\r\n        };\r\n\r\n        myEmitter.on(\"my-event\", handler);\r\n\r\n        return () => {\r\n          myEmitter.off(\"my-event\", handler);\r\n        };\r\n      });\r\n    }),\r\n  });\r\n};\r\n\r\n// WRONG for trpc-electron - async generators don't work with IPC transport\r\nexport const createMyRouter = () => {\r\n  return router({\r\n    subscribe: publicProcedure.subscription(async function* () {\r\n      // This will NOT work - the generator never gets invoked\r\n      while (true) {\r\n        yield await getNextEvent();\r\n      }\r\n    }),\r\n  });\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verifying renderer changes via CDP\r\n\r\nTo check a change end-to-end against the real API/DB, drive the running dev app over CDP. Launch with an unused port, for example `RENDERER_REMOTE_DEBUG_PORT=9222 bun dev` (full stack; the app may restore a signed-in session), then attach via the page target's `webSocketDebuggerUrl` over a WebSocket (Bun built-in, no deps). Example: `scripts/cdp-smoke-integrations.ts`.\r\n\r\n**Never assume port 9222 or attach to a renderer from another worktree.** Multiple Superset workspaces commonly run at once, each with different renderer, API, and CDP ports. Before testing:\r\n\r\n1. Read this workspace's final `DESKTOP_VITE_PORT` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` values from the root `.env`.\r\n2. Find the Electron process whose executable/parent command path is inside this workspace. Its renderer command line contains `--remote-debugging-port=<port>`; `lsof -nP -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN` can confirm the owning PID.\r\n3. Fetch `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/json/list` and require a `page` target whose URL uses this workspace's `DESKTOP_VITE_PORT`. A responding CDP endpoint alone is not sufficient proof that it belongs to this branch.\r\n4. Pass the matched values explicitly when using a script, e.g. `RENDERER_REMOTE_DEBUG_PORT=<port> NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=<api-origin> bun run apps/desktop/scripts/cdp-smoke-integrations.ts`.\r\n\r\nVerify `/api/auth/get-session` from inside the matched renderer before testing.\r\n\r\n### Repairing CDP auth\r\n\r\nCheck which setup script provisioned the workspace before repairing auth:\r\n\r\n- `.superset/setup.local.sh` creates a per-workspace local stack and runs the idempotent `bun run db:seed-dev`, but intentionally leaves sign-in as a separate step. If the account may be missing, rerun `bun run db:seed-dev` while the local DB stack is running.\r\n- `.superset/setup.sh` seeds `superset-dev-data/auth-token.enc` from `$HOME/.superset/auth-token.enc` when available. Rerunning it without `--force` can fill a missing token. Do not use `--force` merely to repair auth: it resets `superset-dev-data/` before reseeding.\r\n\r\nThe desktop hydrates a persisted token into an in-memory bearer-token closure. A raw `Runtime.evaluate` `fetch` cannot read that closure, and the local-dev sign-in button persists a bearer token but uses `credentials: \"omit\"`; neither guarantees the cookie required by a raw CDP probe. For a workspace created by `setup.local.sh`, repair the CDP session as follows:\r\n\r\n1. Require a localhost API origin; never send dev credentials to a remote or shared API.\r\n2. From `apps/desktop` (so workspace imports resolve), import `DEV_EMAIL` and `DEV_PASSWORD` from `@superset/shared/dev-credentials`; do not copy their literal values into scripts or logs.\r\n3. Through `Runtime.evaluate` in the matched renderer, POST them to `${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/auth/sign-in/email` with JSON content type and `credentials: \"include\"`. Do not print the returned token or response body.\r\n4. Re-fetch `/api/auth/get-session` with `credentials: \"include\"` and require both `session` and `session.activeOrganizationId` before running the test.\r\n\r\nThis credentialed local-dev sign-in creates the browser session cookie needed by subsequent in-renderer fetches. If it fails, report the sign-in/session status codes only. For a non-local setup, use the app's normal sign-in flow; never substitute local dev credentials.\r\n\r\nFor a non-local workspace, the normal desktop flow intentionally restores an encrypted bearer token into the renderer's in-memory auth client without creating a browser cookie. If the renderer is on an authenticated route but a raw cookie-only probe returns no session, use `Runtime.evaluate` to import `/lib/auth-client.ts` from the renderer dev server and call `authClient.getSession({ fetchOptions: { throw: false } })`. This still verifies `/api/auth/get-session` through the app's real authenticated request path. Return only the status and `session.activeOrganizationId`; never call or print `getAuthToken()`.\r\n\r\nDo not use setup `--force` to fix a stale connection string, a missing CDP cookie, or a corrupt generated Next.js cache. First rerun the applicable setup script without force. If every API route returns Next.js's HTML 404, stop the dev stack, move `apps/api/.next` aside, and restart. `--force` is only appropriate when the user explicitly intends to replace the copied local/host databases and encrypted auth token.\r\n\r\nOne failure signature where `./.superset/setup.sh --force` IS the fix (verified 2026-07-28): session restore hangs at \"Restoring your session\", the Local Admin sign-in button returns a bodyless 500, get-session returns 200, and a raw `select 1` against `DATABASE_URL` may still succeed — the worktree's seeded dev state (Neon branch credentials in `.env`, `auth-token.enc`, copied DBs) has gone stale as a set. Rerunning with `--force` recreates the Neon branch, rewrites `.env`, and reseeds `superset-dev-data/` together, which restores sign-in. Two side effects to expect: any manual `.env` edits (e.g. a port remap) are wiped and must be re-applied, and `superset-dev-data/` is reset.\r\n\r\n**Use `Runtime.evaluate` (`awaitPromise`, `returnByValue`), not `Network.*` interception** — sniffing misses React-Query-cached responses, and `refetchInterval` is paused while the window is backgrounded. After verifying the session through the applicable cookie or bearer path above, run requests inside the renderer. `API` below is the dev backend origin (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, e.g. `http://localhost:5881`):\r\n\r\n- Active org: local cookie flow uses `fetch(API + \"/api/auth/get-session\", {credentials:\"include\"})`; non-local bearer flow uses `authClient.getSession({ fetchOptions: { throw: false } })`. Require `.session.activeOrganizationId`.\r\n- A tRPC query (bypasses the cache): GET `API + \"/api/trpc/<proc>?batch=1&input=\" + encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify({\"0\":{json:<input>}}))`; response is `[{result:{data:{json:...}}}]`.\r\n- `window.location.hash` nav may not remount the route — call the endpoint directly instead.\r\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false,"parent":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\CLAUDE.md"},"displayPath":"apps\\desktop\\AGENTS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9be3e800-f5e9-45ff-b4ea-16ce1edc7bed","timestamp":"2026-08-12T18:55:33.006Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"9be3e800-f5e9-45ff-b4ea-16ce1edc7bed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_09797a3f9af91050016a7cc1ac103c8191930b4e5cc9910e4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9084,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":228096,"output_tokens":101,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_L7PWyfX6jWv08ggeXE6RMkdM","name":"Grep","input":{"path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\src\\main\\lib\\agent-jsonl-watcher\\pane-map-hook.ts","pattern":"def _teammate|def _filter|TEAM-ENTRY|teamstate|droppable =|idle_notification","output_mode":"content","-n":true,"context":12,"head_limit":340}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"cd58f08b-4ec0-4d54-b3e4-47bdb9005078","timestamp":"2026-08-12T18:55:44.329Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"cd58f08b-4ec0-4d54-b3e4-47bdb9005078","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b87aaebb-d522-4c34-973b-070662a5ef4a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_L7PWyfX6jWv08ggeXE6RMkdM","type":"tool_result","content":"437-            h.write(line + \"\\\\n\")\n438-    except Exception:\n439-        pass\n440-\n441-\n442-def _read_payload():\n443-    candidates = []\n444-    try:\n445-        # (HOOK-STDIN-UTF8) UTF-8-decode the raw bytes: Windows text-mode\n446-        # stdin decodes cp1252 and mojibakes non-ASCII payload chars. Captured\n447-        # live 2026-07-28: a teammate background_tasks description's em-dash\n448-        # (U+2014, 3 UTF-8 bytes) arrived as 3 cp1252 chars, so the\n449:        # (TEAM-ENTRY-MATCH) prefix match against the correctly-decoded\n450-        # transcript prompt failed on that one entry forever -> the lead\n451-        # terminal's dot latched yellow with zero agents running. Strict\n452-        # decode first (payloads are harness-emitted JSON, always valid\n453-        # UTF-8); on the never-expected failure, log loud and fall back to\n454-        # replacement decoding so the hook still POSTs the lifecycle event.\n455-        data = sys.stdin.buffer.read()\n456-        try:\n457-            raw = data.decode(\"utf-8\")\n458-        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n459-            try:\n460-                _log({\n461-                    \"action\": \"payload-decode-error\",\n--\n545-    # long-lived teammate, or one that died without a clean SubagentStop, to a\n546-    # finished status). Refreshed ONLY on genuine forward activity (never on the\n547-    # hold itself, which would keep it perpetually fresh); the JSONL watcher\n548-    # re-asserts yellow within its poll if a reaped set turns out to still write.\n549-    return (\n550-        pathlib.Path.home()\n551-        / \".superset\"\n552-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n553-        / (terminal_id + \".bgactive\")\n554-    )\n555-\n556-\n557:def _teamstate_path(terminal_id):\n558-    # (TEAMMATE-IDLE) incremental parse cache for the lead transcript's\n559-    # teammate ledger plus named-fork tool-use mapping. Versioned so a schema\n560-    # change forces a full reparse and heals entries written by older code.\n561-    # Keyed by transcript path, so a /resume (new transcript file) or terminalId\n562-    # reuse also self-invalidates. Corruption tolerated: any read failure falls\n563-    # back to offset 0 — self-healing, never trusted blindly.\n564-    return (\n565-        pathlib.Path.home()\n566-        / \".superset\"\n567-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n568:        / (terminal_id + \".teamstate.json\")\n569-    )\n570-\n571-\n572-def _askq_dir(terminal_id):\n573-    # (UNTAGGED-BG-RED) a DIRECTORY of per-owner \"an AskUserQuestion is pending\"\n574-    # markers for this terminal — one file per owner (the raising agent). An\n575-    # AskUserQuestion red's ONLY valid clear is its own answer\n576-    # (PostToolUse:AskUserQuestion) or that owner's turn boundary — NEVER a\n577-    # generic main-loop tool completion. While ANY marker exists an untagged\n578-    # ordinary PostToolUse asserts working WITHOUT clearing the red, so a\n579-    # teammate/fork's parent-attributed (agent_id-less) tool cannot stomp a\n580-    # still-open question. Keyed PER OWNER (not one terminal-wide flag) so two\n--\n935-            has_shell = True\n936-        else:\n937-            has_agent = True\n938-    return (has_any, has_agent, has_shell)\n939-\n940-\n941-# (TEAMMATE-IDLE) Claude Code NEVER flips an idle teammate's background_tasks[]\n942-# entry off \"running\" (captured live 2026-07-10: 33 teammate entries, all\n943-# status \"running\", for a session whose 44 teammates had ALL finished hours\n944-# earlier), so the payload alone cannot green a lead whose teammates are done —\n945-# once no further hook event arrived, the dot stayed yellow forever. The lead\n946-# TRANSCRIPT has the missing truth: every teammate that finishes delivers an\n947:# idle_notification teammate-message into it, and every (re)activation is\n948-# visible too (an Agent spawn tool_use, a SendMessage tool_use to it, a\n949-# non-idle teammate-message/agent-message from it).\n950-#\n951:# (TEAM-ENTRY-MATCH) The original all-idle predicate (drop teammate entries\n952-# only when EVERY tracked name is idle) proved unsatisfiable in real sessions\n953-# (captured live 2026-07-22: 55 permanently-\"active\" names — named non-fork\n954-# Agent spawns like sol/general-purpose review agents that finish via\n955-# task-notification and never idle-notify, forks re-marked active by a later\n956-# SendMessage, and \"name [hash]\" duplicate-suffix splits — held 25 finished\n957-# wrangler teammates yellow all day). The decision is now PER ENTRY: a\n958-# running teammate entry's payload \"description\" is the spawn prompt's head\n959-# (observed live: first 50 chars + \"...\"), so match it against the prompt\n960-# prefix recorded at each named Agent spawn; an entry may be dropped only\n961-# when it matches at least one recorded spawn AND every matching name's last\n962:# ledger event is an idle_notification. Unmatched, ambiguous-with-active, or\n963-# unparseable -> keep that entry (the safe yellow direction). Poisoned\n964-# \"active\" names can no longer block OTHER teammates' drops. A teammate that\n965-# dies WITHOUT ever reporting stays \"active\" and keeps its own hold: from\n966-# the logs that case is indistinguishable from a long think, so it is\n967-# deliberately left to (BG-STALE).\n968-\n969-\n970-def _team_norm(text):\n971-    # Collapse whitespace runs to single spaces so a spawn prompt and the\n972-    # payload description derived from it compare equal even if truncation\n973-    # or the harness normalized newlines. String ops only (NO regex: this\n974-    # file is a TS template literal and single backslashes in regex escapes\n975-    # would be silently swallowed).\n976-    return \" \".join(str(text or \"\").split())\n977-\n978-\n979-def _team_scan_text(state, text):\n980-    # Update the name -> \"active\"|\"idle\" ledger from one transcript text blob.\n981-    # String scanning only (NO regex): this file is a TS template literal, and\n982-    # single backslashes in regex escapes would be silently swallowed.\n983:    # (TEAM-ENTRY-MATCH) A duplicate teammate name is delivered with a\n984-    # \" [hash]\" suffix in its messages while the spawn recorded the base name;\n985-    # mirror every suffixed update onto the base key so the base key tracks\n986-    # the LATEST same-named instance instead of latching a stale idle.\n987-    # Accepted narrow risk (review 2026-07-22): same name + identical prompt\n988-    # head + the OLD instance silently working when the new one idles can\n989-    # false-green the old entry until its next message re-actives the base.\n990-    i = 0\n991-    tag = '<teammate-message teammate_id=\"'\n992-    while True:\n993-        i = text.find(tag, i)\n994-        if i < 0:\n995-            break\n996-        j = i + len(tag)\n997-        k = text.find('\"', j)\n998-        if k < 0:\n999-            break\n1000-        name = text[j:k]\n1001-        end = text.find(\"</teammate-message>\", k)\n1002-        body = text[k:end] if end > 0 else text[k:]\n1003-        if name:\n1004:            val = \"idle\" if '\"idle_notification\"' in body else \"active\"\n1005-            state[name] = val\n1006-            if \" [\" in name:\n1007-                base = name.split(\" [\")[0].strip()\n1008-                if base:\n1009-                    state[base] = val\n1010-        i = k\n1011-    a = 0\n1012-    tag2 = '<agent-message from=\"'\n1013-    while True:\n1014-        a = text.find(tag2, a)\n1015-        if a < 0:\n1016-            break\n--\n1044-    k = text.find(\"</tool-use-id>\", j)\n1045-    if k < 0:\n1046-        return\n1047-    tool_use_id = text[j:k].strip()\n1048-    name = fork_tools.get(tool_use_id)\n1049-    if name:\n1050-        state.pop(name, None)\n1051-\n1052-\n1053-def _team_scan_record(state, fork_tools, prompts, obj):\n1054-    # One JSONL transcript record -> ledger updates. Spawning a non-fork Agent\n1055-    # with a name or waking it via SendMessage marks it active; the spawn also\n1056:    # records a normalized prompt prefix so (TEAM-ENTRY-MATCH) can map a\n1057-    # background_tasks[] teammate entry's description back to this name. Named\n1058-    # forks are excluded and indexed by Agent tool-use-id so a completed\n1059-    # task-notification can untrack stale state; a SendMessage to a known fork\n1060-    # name is IGNORED (forks never idle-notify — marking one active poisoned\n1061-    # the ledger forever, live 2026-07-22). Teammate/agent message text\n1062-    # decides idle vs active.\n1063-    top_content = obj.get(\"content\")\n1064-    if isinstance(top_content, str):\n1065-        _team_scan_completion(state, fork_tools, top_content)\n1066-    msg = obj.get(\"message\") or {}\n1067-    if not isinstance(msg, dict):\n1068-        return\n--\n1113-\n1114-\n1115-def _team_ledger(transcript_path, terminal_id):\n1116-    # Incrementally parse the lead transcript into (state, prompts): name ->\n1117-    # \"active\"|\"idle\" plus name -> normalized spawn-prompt prefix. Consumes\n1118-    # only bytes appended since the cached offset (the first call pays one\n1119-    # full read; transcripts are append-only, surviving /compact). Cache\n1120-    # schema v3 (adds prompts) — an older cache fails the version check and\n1121-    # forces one full rescan, self-healing already-poisoned ledgers. Never\n1122-    # raises; every failure path returns None (keep every hold).\n1123-    if not transcript_path or not terminal_id:\n1124-        return None\n1125:    cache_file = _teamstate_path(terminal_id)\n1126-    state = {}\n1127-    fork_tools = {}\n1128-    prompts = {}\n1129-    offset = 0\n1130-    try:\n1131-        rec = json.loads(cache_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n1132-        if (\n1133-            isinstance(rec, dict)\n1134-            and rec.get(\"version\") == 3\n1135-            and rec.get(\"path\") == transcript_path\n1136-            and isinstance(rec.get(\"state\"), dict)\n1137-            and isinstance(rec.get(\"forkTools\"), dict)\n--\n1183-                \"state\": state,\n1184-                \"forkTools\": fork_tools,\n1185-                \"prompts\": prompts,\n1186-            }),\n1187-            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n1188-        )\n1189-    except Exception:\n1190-        pass\n1191-    return (state, prompts)\n1192-\n1193-\n1194-def _team_entry_droppable(entry, state, prompts):\n1195:    # (TEAM-ENTRY-MATCH) True only on POSITIVE proof for THIS entry: its\n1196-    # description (spawn-prompt head, \"...\"-truncated) matches at least one\n1197-    # recorded spawn prompt AND every matching name's last ledger event is an\n1198:    # idle_notification. Identical prompt prefixes across teammates simply\n1199-    # widen the match set — then ALL of them must be idle. Too-short or\n1200-    # unmatched descriptions never drop (the safe yellow direction).\n1201-    desc = str(entry.get(\"description\") or \"\")\n1202-    if desc.endswith(\"...\"):\n1203-        desc = desc[: len(desc) - 3]\n1204-    prefix = _team_norm(desc)\n1205-    if len(prefix) < 12:\n1206-        return False\n1207-    names = []\n1208-    for name, p in prompts.items():\n1209-        if p and p.startswith(prefix):\n1210-            names.append(name)\n--\n1258-        \"reason\": reason,\n1259-        \"prefix_len\": len(prefix),\n1260-        \"prefix\": prefix[:220],\n1261-        \"matches\": matches,\n1262-        \"ledger_state\": {str(k): str(v) for k, v in state.items()},\n1263-        \"entry\": {str(k): str(v)[:300] for k, v in entry.items()},\n1264-    }\n1265-    with open(log_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as h:\n1266-        h.write(json.dumps(rec) + \"\\\\n\")\n1267-\n1268-\n