{"parentUuid":"16ed7d7a-e998-4784-845b-da1f11d0c3f3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_032de7d51ea8b9db016a7cc20bc0d881918fbae134d2351a36","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":241408,"output_tokens":227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_s6efmOsgH2qS1tyjRtwLp0Bn","name":"Grep","input":{"path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\src\\main\\lib\\agent-jsonl-watcher\\pane-map-hook.ts","pattern":"_BG_STALE_SECONDS|bgactive|stale agent|agent-type","output_mode":"content","-n":true,"context":14,"head_limit":260}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"0e92cca2-fb61-4212-b93e-f45a332d6ef5","timestamp":"2026-08-12T18:57:22.284Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"0e92cca2-fb61-4212-b93e-f45a332d6ef5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b87aaebb-d522-4c34-973b-070662a5ef4a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_s6efmOsgH2qS1tyjRtwLp0Bn","type":"tool_result","content":"310-const NOTIFY_SCRIPT = `#!/usr/bin/env python3\n311-\"\"\"Superset Claude agent-status notify hook.\n312-\n313-Installed by agent-jsonl-watcher/pane-map-hook.ts. POSTs each Claude lifecycle\n314-event to the host-service (SUPERSET_HOST_AGENT_HOOK_URL) so the agent-status\n315-dots are driven event-driven — reviving what the dead bash notify.sh did.\n316-\n317-Event -> eventType mapping (NEVER defaults to Stop on an unknown event; an\n318-unmapped event is a silent no-op, exactly like notify.sh):\n319-  UserPromptSubmit            -> Start            (working / yellow)\n320-  Stop                        -> Stop             (review/green) UNLESS a\n321-                                 subagent is still running (then suppressed —\n322-                                 stay yellow; greens on the last SubagentStop).\n323-                                 With background_tasks[] still running, the\n324:                                 entry TYPES decide: any agent-type entry\n325-                                 (subagent/teammate/workflow) -> SubagentActive\n326-                                 (yellow; red-respecting in the renderer);\n327-                                 shell-only -> BackgroundRunning (blue)\n328-  SessionEnd                  -> Stop             (review / green; clears state)\n329-  StopFailure(main loop)      -> Stop + clears state, UNLESS a codex-companion\n330-                                 job for this session is still alive ->\n331-                                 SubagentActive (BF: codex runs on its OWN API;\n332-                                 a Claude rate-limit abort does not stop it)\n333-  StopFailure(in a subagent)  -> (STOPFAIL-SUBAGENT) self-scoped: drops only that\n334-                                 fork's markers, never the shared session state /\n335-                                 the main question guard; the central red guard\n336-                                 keeps a still-pending AskUserQuestion red\n337-  Notification                -> PermissionRequest (permission / red)\n338-  PreToolUse(AskUserQuestion) -> PermissionRequest (red)   else no-op\n--\n350-                                 — superset-notify.py owns it; notify.sh no longer does)\n351-  SubagentStart               -> SubagentActive   (working, red-respecting — a\n352-                                 workflow/teammate spawning an agent while a red\n353-                                 is pending must not stomp it; the subagent\n354-                                 marker still holds yellow through the main Stop)\n355-  SubagentStop                -> Stop iff it was the LAST subagent AND main had\n356-                                 already stopped, else no-op (see _decide_event_type)\n357-  PreCompact                  -> Start            (working — context compaction is\n358-                                 a minutes-long LLM call during which no other\n359-                                 hook fires; manual /compact does not even fire\n360-                                 UserPromptSubmit, verified live)\n361-  SessionStart(source=compact)-> Stop after a MANUAL compact (same decision as\n362-                                 Stop, so the subagent yellow-hold is respected\n363-                                 and the persisted turn-end snapshot markers\n364:                                 restore yellow for agent-type background work\n365-                                 or BLUE for a still-running background shell);\n366-                                 re-asserts Start after an AUTO compact (the turn\n367-                                 is still live); no-op when we never marked a\n368-                                 compact as running\n369-\n370-Server maps Start->working, Stop->review, PermissionRequest->permission and\n371-returns {\"result\":{\"data\":{\"json\":{\"success\":true,...}}}}. Uses only stdlib\n372-urllib so it has no third-party dependency. Silent on every failure path — a\n373-broken hook must NEVER raise or abort the agent.\n374-\n375-(COMPANION-CAPTURE) The POST body additionally carries the whole\n376-AskUserQuestion payload — companionQuestion on PreToolUse, and\n377-companionQuestionResolved on the matching PostToolUse — so the companion\n378-bridge can render a question on a phone/watch and retract the notification\n--\n496-\n497-def _compact_marker_path(terminal_id):\n498-    # (COMPACT-YELLOW) records \"a compaction is running\" plus its trigger\n499-    # (manual|auto) so the finish path knows how to clear the dot.\n500-    return (\n501-        pathlib.Path.home()\n502-        / \".superset\"\n503-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n504-        / (terminal_id + \".compacting\")\n505-    )\n506-\n507-\n508-def _agentbg_marker_path(terminal_id):\n509-    # (TEAM-YELLOW) records \"the latest Stop/SubagentStop snapshot saw\n510:    # agent-type background work still running\". Consumed by the manual-compact\n511-    # finish path, whose SessionStart payload carries NO background_tasks of\n512-    # its own — without it, /compact ending while teammates/workflows run\n513-    # would false-green. Refreshed from every turn-end payload; a stale marker\n514-    # errs yellow (safe) and clears at the next bg-free turn end.\n515-    return (\n516-        pathlib.Path.home()\n517-        / \".superset\"\n518-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n519-        / (terminal_id + \".agentbg\")\n520-    )\n521-\n522-\n523-def _shellbg_marker_path(terminal_id):\n524-    # Sibling of .agentbg for the BLUE direction: records \"the latest\n525-    # Stop/SubagentStop snapshot saw ONLY shell-type background work still\n526-    # running\". Consumed by the same manual-compact finish path so /compact\n527-    # ending while a background shell runs restores the BackgroundRunning\n528-    # blue instead of false-greening (verified live 2026-06-11). A stale\n529-    # marker errs blue-lingers — the same accepted (BA)/(BE) tradeoff — and\n530-    # clears at the next turn end.\n531-    return (\n532-        pathlib.Path.home()\n533-        / \".superset\"\n534-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n535-        / (terminal_id + \".shellbg\")\n536-    )\n537-\n538-\n539:def _bgactive_marker_path(terminal_id):\n540-    # (BG-STALE) Last time REAL teammate/subagent activity was seen for this\n541-    # terminal (a SubagentStart or a subagent-scoped PostToolUse). Consulted at a\n542-    # turn-end agent-hold: an agent set Claude Code still reports \"running\" but\n543:    # that has produced no activity for _BG_STALE_SECONDS is idle/zombie and must\n544-    # stop pinning the lead's dot yellow (the harness never flips an idle\n545-    # long-lived teammate, or one that died without a clean SubagentStop, to a\n546-    # finished status). Refreshed ONLY on genuine forward activity (never on the\n547-    # hold itself, which would keep it perpetually fresh); the JSONL watcher\n548-    # re-asserts yellow within its poll if a reaped set turns out to still write.\n549-    return (\n550-        pathlib.Path.home()\n551-        / \".superset\"\n552-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n553:        / (terminal_id + \".bgactive\")\n554-    )\n555-\n556-\n557-def _teamstate_path(terminal_id):\n558-    # (TEAMMATE-IDLE) incremental parse cache for the lead transcript's\n559-    # teammate ledger plus named-fork tool-use mapping. Versioned so a schema\n560-    # change forces a full reparse and heals entries written by older code.\n561-    # Keyed by transcript path, so a /resume (new transcript file) or terminalId\n562-    # reuse also self-invalidates. Corruption tolerated: any read failure falls\n563-    # back to offset 0 — self-healing, never trusted blindly.\n564-    return (\n565-        pathlib.Path.home()\n566-        / \".superset\"\n567-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n--\n1439-            \"reaped\": reaped,\n1440-            \"boundSeconds\": _MARKER_STALE_SECONDS,\n1441-        })\n1442-    return remaining\n1443-\n1444-\n1445-# (BG-STALE) Seconds of ZERO teammate/subagent activity after which a\n1446-# background_tasks[] agent set that Claude Code still reports \"running\" is\n1447-# treated as idle/zombie and stops pinning the lead's dot yellow. Claude Code\n1448-# never flips an idle long-lived teammate (or one that died without a clean\n1449-# SubagentStop) to a finished status, so without this the dot stays yellow until\n1450-# the team is disbanded \\ the session ends (live incident 2026-06-24: 6\n1451-# teammates \"running\" but silent 27 min). 15 min is long enough that a team\n1452-# doing real work — which streams SubagentStart / subagent-scoped PostToolUse\n1453:# events that refresh .bgactive — never ages out, while a stalled set recovers\n1454-# quickly; the JSONL watcher re-asserts yellow within its poll if a reaped set\n1455-# is in fact still writing, so the reap errs recoverable, not permanent.\n1456:_BG_STALE_SECONDS = 900\n1457-\n1458-\n1459-def _bg_hold_is_stale(terminal_id):\n1460:    # True iff .bgactive exists and is older than _BG_STALE_SECONDS (the held\n1461-    # agent set has shown no activity that long). A MISSING marker is NOT stale:\n1462-    # the caller seeds it at the turn-end snapshot and holds yellow once, so a\n1463-    # team that predates this code (no SubagentStart seen) still gets a single\n1464-    # benefit-of-the-doubt turn before it can be reaped. Any error -> NOT stale\n1465-    # (the safe yellow direction). Never raises.\n1466:    p = _bgactive_marker_path(terminal_id)\n1467-    try:\n1468-        import time\n1469:        return (time.time() - p.stat().st_mtime) > _BG_STALE_SECONDS\n1470-    except Exception:\n1471-        return False\n1472-\n1473-\n1474-def _decide_event_type(\n1475-    event,\n1476