{"parentUuid":"8b446677-d075-46aa-b235-6a740afad463","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdyVyGfYfwoukhimCSBYa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JJE5c2nWkmBxiPmFFgCAfk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Post-install pacing E2E verification","name":"postinstall-pacing-e2e","prompt":"Post-install verification of Superset desktop 1.20.2 (commit 7b56fc6fa, companion answer inter-frame pacing fix) on this Windows ARM64 machine. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64. The app was just installed and the PC restarted; Superset is running (PIDs started 21:34).\n\nGoal (task #5): prove the multi-question phone-answer path now works end-to-end on the INSTALLED build, using an emulated companion client with a DISTINCT paired identity.\n\nHard constraints:\n- NEVER reuse the physical phone's paired device identity or keys. Last time a scratch emulator reused it and its reduced-capability hello broke the phone's FCM registration. Create a NEW paired identity via a fresh pairing window.\n- Never log or persist free-text bodies, keys, tokens, QR secrets, or transcript content. The pairing secret lives only in memory/scratch process state.\n- All scratch files under C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\ (gitignored). Do not modify production code. Do not commit or push.\n- Do not touch the physical phone's registration or send it capability-changing hellos.\n\nSteps:\n1. Verify the installed build's host-service companion bridge is up: check C:\\Users\\khair\\.superset\\host\\*\\host-service.log (newest session dir) for bridge listening + no companion errors since 21:34 local. Verify the installed app bundle contains the pacing change (grep the installed host-service bundle under C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\resources for ANSWER_INTER_FRAME_DELAY or ANSWER-FRAME-PACING).\n2. Create a distinct emulator identity: call the desktop's authenticated tRPC openPairing (loopback; prior scratch harnesses in tmp\\phone-emu\\ and tmp\\ show the shape — pre-guardless-answer.ts / safe-e2e.ts are references but they used the PHONE identity; write a NEW pairing+hello client that derives fresh device keys and registers as a full-capability device labelled 'e2e-emulator'). The pairing window is 120s on port 47611; complete pairing within it. Log only pairingRef.\n3. Start a controlled Claude Code terminal INSIDE Superset's host-service (or use the pty-daemon path the bridge writes to — the question must be captured by the real hook path so it appears in /v1/tree). Simplest proven approach: run a real claude.exe session in a Superset terminal workspace via the host-service, prompt it to call AskUserQuestion once with exactly four single-select synthetic canary questions (headers CanaryOne..CanaryFou, options AlphaN/BetaN — synthetic labels only). Wait for the question to appear as pending via the sealed /v1/tree//v1/question read path.\n4. Answer all four questions in ONE sealed /v1/answer request from the emulator identity (select answers: Beta1, Alpha2, Beta3, Alpha4). Then poll /v1/answer/status and the question store.\n5. PASS criteria: protocol-v3 confirmed outcome; each inter-frame gap ~500ms visible in timing (answer takes ~2s not ~100ms); the Claude transcript's AskUserQuestion tool_result contains ALL FOUR answers correctly attributed; question settles resolved with phone provenance only after the tool_result. The tool_result is the ONLY ground truth — ledger 'confirmed' alone is not a pass.\n6. Report: bridge health, bundle pacing evidence, pairing outcome (pairingRef only), answer request timing, ledger outcome, tool_result verdict per question, and any anomalies. If any step is blocked (e.g. pairing needs UI interaction you cannot drive), stop and report exactly what is blocked rather than working around it unsafely.\n\nEnvironment notes: SUPERSET_HOST_AGENT_HOOK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:48056/trpc/notifications.hook (may change after restart — re-derive from the running host-service). bun is at ~/.bun/bin (not on Git-bash PATH by default). Claude CLI 2.1.228 at C:/Users/khair/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-code/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-code-win32-arm64/claude.exe. Prior proof harness for the 4-question picker: tmp\\pty-proof-4q\\proof-4q.mjs (that one drives claude directly, NOT through the bridge — steps 3-5 must go through the bridge).","subagent_type":"claude"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_read_input_tokens":416633,"output_tokens":2389,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":612},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2389,"cache_read_input_tokens":416633,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"fdaa5c3e-8563-4a8f-8efe-3a88760c42ea","timestamp":"2026-08-12T20:40:16.093Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
